    38	## #30 — Between-books items from the Monroe 1.3 Book 1 ending (default in force)
    39	Book 1 (edition) ends with Darrow saying he'll be "back up this river in the autumn… he'll want to know" and Feryn's coat "I'll not see it till the autumn". Book 2's map keeps Darrow as Book 1 history only and Feryn off-page. **Default: lapse both** — at most one memory line each in Book 2; neither is staged. Owner may instead ask for a short Darrow return in Book 2's autumn circuit.
    40	
    41	## #31 — Coss's senior flag date (resolved by edition canon)
    42	Book 2's map: "three days after the Darrow fight". Edition Book 1: dated the day after. **The edition governs: the day after.**
    43	
    44	## #32 — Audio hosting for the Monroe 1.3 edition (OWNER, 2026-10-03)
    45	Breeze renders live in the **fractured-path repo via Git LFS**, beside the current edition's ElevenLabs audio, under new edition ids. 64 kbps mono mp3.
    46	
    47	## #33 — Pronunciations (OWNER-CONFIRMED, 2026-10-03)
    48	- **Cael** = KAYL, one syllable (rhymes with "sail"). Render spelling "Kale".
    49	- **Lira** = LEER-a. Render spelling "Leera".
    50	All other names in the listening proof's lexicon (`book-01-the-shattered/state/completion/listening-proof.md` §4) remain proposals (unconfirmed; not substituted at render).
    51	
    52	## #34 — Breeze licence and publication (OWNER, 2026-10-03)
    53	Publish the edition in books.worker-bee.app labeled exactly as Meridian is: "Listening audition, not production-approved; Breeze licence is non-commercial."
    54	
    55	## #35 — B4 month arithmetic (coordinator flag, 2026-10-05; extends C8 / BOOK_MAP §11)
    56	The edition's Book 4 calendar (closed M4: the Fiske bout ≈d141, Fiske's protected "Six weeks. I'll see you in the final.") puts the eleventh of Sowing (Cael's birthday, ≈d167) about sixteen days before the Copper final and the semester evaluation, which the plan dates in Reaping (inspection from "the twelfth day of Reaping"; the evaluation "the twentieth of Reaping"). Sixteen days cannot span from an eleventh to a nineteenth/twentieth of a different, ordinary-length month.
    57	**DEFAULT in force:** the prose never states month lengths, which month follows which, or a day count between a Sowing date and a Reaping date; day counts are stated only in days/weeks from events. The protected Sowing/Reaping dates stand. Owner may later rule the series calendar (e.g. Reaping as the month after Sowing with a shorter feast-month between, or moving the birthday earlier). Does not block.
    58	
    59	**#35 update (coordinator, 2026-10-05, B4 M5 review).** The plan's own protected lines collided: M4's "Six weeks. I'll see you in the final." (closed, published) vs the M5 closing Log's "Semester evaluation in nine weeks." Ruling: the Log now reads "seventeen days" (BOOK_MAP §9 amended). With the final on the nineteenth of Reaping and the evaluation on the twentieth, M6–M7's events fit the seventeen days (semifinal ≈ the tenth, nine days before the final; delegation the twelfth/thirteenth). The one residue is the birthday's month name: "the eleventh of Sowing" falls about sixteen days before the nineteenth of Reaping. The DEFAULT above stands (never state month order or a cross-month day count). Owner options: accept short months / an intercalary feast-week; or move the birthday to "the third of Reaping" (B5's recollection would follow).
    60	
    61	## #36 — Book 2 → Book 3 hand-off conflicts (coordinator, 2026-10-05; B2 M8 author flags)
    62	The closed, hash-locked edition Book 3 says some things the Book 2 plan contradicts. Defaults in force:
    63	1. **Redirect shoulder.** B3 ch1:111 says Pressure-adjacent's three clean uses are "each paid for in the right shoulder"; B3 ch1:45 says "his own right shoulder, the one the Reydan bout had already used hard". B2 M7 (closed) drilled the redirect on the LEFT (ch47:117, ch51:159). **Default:** Book 2 conforms to Book 3. The two M7 lines become "right" as a coordinator erratum, and M8's bout pays every redirect in the right shoulder. Book 2 is not locked yet; Book 3 stays untouched.
    64	2. **Track name.** B3 ch1:296 has the gate clerk say "observer track"; B2 calls it the "demonstration-provision track". **Default:** in B2 M8, Quenna or Cael uses both names once ("the demonstration-provision track; the observer track, on the gate list"). Book 3 is untouched.
    65	3. **Exchange and notice timing.** B3 ch35:227 has "in the third exchange of the bout" and "the notice had come at the very last moment". The B2 map has the fourth exchange, with the notice after the final low-stakes bout (§8 item 8). **Default:** B2 keeps its map. A B3 erratum is QUEUED: "third exchange" → "fourth exchange", and "the notice had come" → "the thing had come", or similar wording for the arrival. It will be applied in one Book 3 v1.1 re-lock pass (re-hash, new DIRECTOR_CUT_READY, new tag) after Book 2 locks.
    66	4. **Season.** B3 ch1:136 says "Early autumn"; ch9 says the Reydan entry reached Karis "in the first days of autumn". The B2 map says "name no months; keep departure before hard winter", and the B2 M8 draft has frost on the departure morning and "before the first snow". **Default:** B2 ch60's departure morning names no season and shows no frost or snow. Quenna's warning becomes "before the weather turns on the hill road". Book 3 stands as written. The owner may later rule on the series calendar.
    67	5. **Log format.** B3 uses four headings per fragment. B2 M8 begins that format with the Compression entry, and Cael means to redo the older three on the road. Accepted.
    68	
    69	**#36 update (coordinator, 2026-10-05, after the B2 M8 Fable reviews).** The redirect side is confirmed RIGHT. Book 3 says so consistently (ch1:45, ch1:111, ch6:91, ch6:201), so Book 2 conforms: the M7 side-words become right, and so do the M8 bout redirects and the Compression channel. The Book 3 erratum queue (v1.1 re-lock after Book 2 locks) is now: ch22 and ch35:227 "third exchange" → "fourth exchange", and the notice "had come" during the bout → the arrival of the thing itself (the notice comes after the final bout). Book 3 ch1's loose "weeks" stands.
