   343	*(Refreshed after repair r1.)*
   344	
   345	**Calendar.** A little before noon on the **two hundred and eighty-first day past the Line**, going down the western side of the long rise, a day's walk from Treswick. Days on the page: 278, 279, 280, 281. No season, month or weekday name; no figures for the technician's date; no count of years since the Kindling.
   346	
   347	**Where everyone is.** Six going down off the rise: Seln in front, Lira, Brom, Karis, and then **Cael with Vastin walking beside him on the ditch side** (from the top of the rise; nobody asked him to and nobody told him no). Oryn and the brown mule went north from the fork at first light and did not look back. Teague's five are east of the river.
   348	
   349	**Cael.** Nineteen. **Ten fragments; no eleventh.** **Deployment thirty-two.** Left palm stung by Ember. He ruled on a job and has made no vow. **He has read the technician's date, laid it against the first line of his own file, and knows it for the day of his own Kindling. He has not written it, has told nobody, and has put no verb to it.** He said "You do now" to Vastin at the hold. He has written in the log, at Oryn's asking, that inside Treswick he does not go near the station. **He has laid his hand on the page once, on the rise, and Karis has it again.** He has seen the light on the crown and turned from it. He carries a box. He asked "Who's Cleon?" and has the name.
   350	
   351	**Lira.** Wind; Iron, Rank One. No burst. **Arm: the sixteenth day out of the wool on the 281st.** It held a hound by the scruff while the right hand struck; it votes; **she carries a box on her back with both arms through its beckets.** Oryn: slow for as long again; don't fall on it. **She no longer has the crossbow.** She knows that Cael has put something away and has not asked.
   352	
   353	**Brom.** Iron Skin; Copper. No grey at any point. Right shoulder still in the older healer's knot (if it tells him anything he is to put the load down and leave it down). **Right foot: two toes bruised, bound; ten days from the 279th, eight left on the 281st.** One box on the left shoulder. He has the purse and Pike's thumbed slip. He lays seven bowls and will carry Oryn's empty.
   354	
   355	**Karis.** Ember; Iron, Rank Three; one point set in the peats. She holds the flat (six rows, counted twice by two people and re-taped, the technician's sheet at the foot of the second), the completion report, the page in its oilcloth inside her coat, her copy, the hide, the kit's ledger and her notebook. She knows: four sign-groups matched to the hide and others matched to nothing, **no number given and none of the others called a place**; five columns; no measure changed in six years; the instruments true; the remark, and that she will not swear to its hand; the box, the same on all four; what an abstract is. She cannot read the index or the box. She began a sentence about lamps and stopped it with her rule, verbatim. She heard "I've read it" from Cael as she had from Seln and asked neither. She named the archive and Cleon. Six findings on her stillhound leaf.
   356	
   357	**Seln.** Shadow; Bronze. One hound with a short knife; "It's clear because it's empty, not because it's safe". **He has read the original date in daylight, has told nobody, and has set the sheet before Cael without a word; he does not know for certain that it was read.** He has taught for the first time ("Draft nothing. Just look.", to Vastin). **He carries no box.** **The case is on him, shut; no ruling upon it.**
   358	
   359	**Oryn.** Tide; Iron, Rank Four, provisional. On Pike's slip as its healer. She asked Vastin and had an explicit yes; shut four holes; bound the joint; two fingers on his wrist. She has priced all six and given Vastin as long as any. **She has not read Cael**: "It's the one thing I'm walking up that road owing, and I'll pay it." She has told the house, the column and why she left, and will not say where. She has her term in his log and has read it there. Gone north with the mule, her linen, and her crossbow with its one bolt; five gates, the ford, then Millrace in three weeks. She does not know that Vastin is carrying the kit's case.
   360	
   361	**Vastin.** No office; **no age stated**. **Iron Wall declared once, on the 279th, in the cut**; spent to the floor. **Right knee: bitten, shut, bound stiff; the 281st is the second day of thirty**; on the stick; no kneeling, running or walls. He qualified every instruction. **He has not sat in front of the crew since the cut.** **He carries the tarred kit case (cord, mallet, stake thirty-two) on the shoulder above his sound leg, taken up unasked at the fork-stone after Oryn had gone, and has told Cael so.** **He walks beside Cael from the top of the rise.** He said the town's name at the spring, the first to say it since the page. He knows the four hands, the doctrine and where a post stands. He has heard the daylight reading whole. **He does not know that the date means anything to anybody**, the mechanism, what Cael carries, the instruments' behaviour in Cael's hand, or what is under the bar; nothing has been said of a directive or an objection. He has not asked to join and nobody has spoken of it.
   362	
   363	**Teague and his crew.** On the east bank; salt going over; then the cold road. He knows the six went west to the cut "and what's beyond it", and that Vastin walks behind them. His term is "where I left it".
   364	
   365	**Pike's book.** Eleven completed lines. The clearance is taken (five strokes and a healer's line) and not yet said closed; **the thumbed slip is in Brom's shirt**. The season line's number still blank. Eleventh on the cloth.
   366	
   367	**Objects and money.** **A hundred and thirty-eight marks.** The reserve sealed. **Owed: sixty yards of four-strand rope to the ferryman.** Three boxes on Brom, Lira and Cael. The kit's case with Vastin. Stake thirty-two never driven. The cord and both edges untouched by Cael since the 168th. Hesk's book has the term on the 280th's leaf and no line for the date.
   368	
   369	**The Quieting, as known.** On paper: the four places of the hide, measured for six years with no change; instruments true inside; one word in the fifth column; one surveyor's remark, and the space for remarks removed afterward; a class mark that is the same on all four. Other sign-groups in the rows, unmatched and uncounted on the page. In the field: unchanged.
   370	
   371	**Who knows what.** The mechanism: six, as before. The daylight reading: the six at the slab, and Oryn by hearing. **The date: Cael and Seln, each alone.** Nobody has interpreted the sequence, said who classed the places or why, or joined the remark to anything or anybody.
   372	
   373	**Words said aloud for the first time.** *Iron Wall* (Vastin, 16:109). The town's name, for the first time since the page (Vastin, 18:215). *Cleon* (Karis, 18:219).
   374	
   375	**Open threads.** A date that two people know and neither has said. "All of it." Sign-groups that are not yet places. A box that nobody can read. A lamps sentence stopped. A knee on its second day, and a case on the shoulder above the other. A reading that a healer owes. Two sentences in a log about a flight of steps and a paved place. A rope of the wrong lay. A question that Cael kept from Vastin at Lowmarch, still kept.
