    26	## Where we enter
    27	
    28	It is the 294th day. The list of parts takes all day, and Cleon's finger is on the last line at the bell. Twelve fragments. Karis's hand is bound and she writes with it anyway. Vastin is on day 15 of a month. There is still no mule.
    29	
    30	## What this movement is for
    31	
    32	The book turns east, on the same road read backwards. Two crews join by contract and not by friendship. Cael watches the Force line in a meadow and does not yet know where it will matter. The grade is cracked, and the sites run oldest-last into the deep edge. At Millrace the healer reads him as deep as she goes. Meanwhile, and against the card, the second instrument turns inward by itself. We are in the last third now: progression surfaces at turning points, and the grade's vocabulary is counted separately (§7.2).
