    40	What asked and was refused: Anchor was silent on the inner stair, and Cael marks it (ch27). The read asked at the dray what it weighed and which way it was going; told no (ch29). In the alley all ten rose; Wind, the read, Ember, Pressure, Anchor and Shadow are named, each told no; Compression rose as Vastin fell and was told no; the catch was made with arms, a box and Brom's bound arm (ch32). Shadow lifted at dusk on the 285th, the 286th and the 290th; told no. Tide was not used on anybody. No self-reading.
    41	
    42	**The acquisition (ch32, scene 4; the notice in ch33, scene 3).** On the 290th, in the cut, with a hood's palm on the plane a yard from his face and four people waiting for him to open something, Cael stands on the eighth step at Vastin's left hip, two feet beneath the plane, and tells ten things no. In that quiet minute "something in him set", as a post is stood in its hole. He did not reach for it. Its question is *This far?* and he tells it no (three times by the movement's end). He reads the lines in the loft. **Not deployed. Not told to Vastin.** Entered in the log, with two lines of his own under the protected entry: *Not told. I can't tell the taking without telling the rest, and the rest is six people's. He asked for the wall to be entered, and I said that it was.* Lira has read the entry and said nothing.
