books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-10.md-39-Not for long. For the length of a man deciding whether a thing he has hoped for and dreaded in equal measure for thirty years is the one or the other, and finding that it is both, and that both is not what the young man who started the work had imagined it would be. He opened them. He looked at the third set, at the Hall's twelve sheets, at a mark on the fourth of them that Cael could not have told from any other mark, and said, quietly, to the sheet and not to Karis:
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-10.md-40-
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-10.md:41:"I know that hand." He did not say from where. "You've brought it in off the ground. Do you know what that is, to a man who's been sitting in a hole for thirty years being tolerated?"
