editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/manuscript/chapter-28.md-85-He wrote it down in the morning at his desk by the window, with his right arm resting on the table because he could not lift it past his ribs, and every deep breath finding the ache under his breastbone and leaning on it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/manuscript/chapter-28.md-86-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/manuscript/chapter-28.md:87:*Compression-adjacent. Brom's room. Full slow push, caught and returned whole, on the eighth try. Done by choosing the whole road first and not changing it. Benefit: none in a real fight yet, but now I know the size of what it can hold. Cost: six breaths gone and a cough, both hands shaking for an hour, right shoulder locked until morning, breastbone too sore to lie on. The sixth try misrouted into the left elbow when I changed the size mid-reach. The price doesn't double with the catch. It more than doubles. Integration: partial. Whole, once.*
