editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/manuscript/chapter-61.md-24-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/manuscript/chapter-61.md-25-*Fragments, confirmed: five.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/manuscript/chapter-61.md-26-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/manuscript/chapter-61.md:27:*Wind-adjacent. Lira. The framework. Still the first thing my feet do when anything comes at me. In the second month Karis asked whether it felt borrowed, and I told her I didn't know. For this one I know now. It isn't borrowed. Lira and I made it between us, in a yard behind a grain exchange, and it lives in me. She's read this page. She agrees, and says Wray is right about the second figure.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/manuscript/chapter-61.md-28-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/manuscript/chapter-61.md:29:*Pressure-adjacent. Feryn. The redirect. Three clean uses mapped, and a price through the shoulder I could count to the breath. I didn't spend it once this term. I still have it. It's the one I think about least and would miss soonest, and I'm putting that down so I'll stop forgetting it.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/manuscript/chapter-61.md-30-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/manuscript/chapter-61.md:31:*Iron-adjacent. Brom. The surface read, from contact out to a few paces, thinner the faster they come. It read through linen and quilting and felt; it gave me Karis's points as weight before they were light. For most of a year I tried to make it be something else. It's better at being what it is.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/manuscript/chapter-61.md-32-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/manuscript/chapter-61.md:33:*Compression-adjacent. Reydan. Taking a push and sending it on. A quarter, a half, a whole slow push, a fast catch, a drop. It carried me across a lit channel and cost me the left arm for a month. I took it from a bout that was a term back now, from the one fighter who ever told me to come and find him when I had the answer. I mean to. That's what this line is for.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/manuscript/chapter-61.md-34-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/manuscript/chapter-61.md:35:*Ember-adjacent. Karis. An ignition point. One channel, at contact or a hair off it. It doesn't glow and it doesn't hold. It lets go, once, and after that the fire belongs to whatever my hand is on. It costs the same whatever size I ask for. Newest of the five, and the only one whose notice carries a line the other four never had.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/manuscript/chapter-61.md-36-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/manuscript/chapter-61.md-37-He wrote that line by itself, under the rest, in the square hand.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/manuscript/chapter-61.md-38-
--
