    59	---
    60	
    61	Cael went out an hour after noon.
    62	
    63	He had not meant to. He had lain on a pallet with his hands behind his head and listened to the street, and he had found that he could not lie under a town which he had not looked at. He had looked at the foot of it for a day. He wished to see how it stood.
    64	
    65	"Which way?" said Lira. She had sat up as soon as his boots moved.
    66	
    67	"Round. Along under the second wall, with the wall on my left hand."
    68	
    69	She saw it at once. With the wall on his left, the hill would be on his left as well; and whatever stood on the crown of the hill would be behind his shoulder for the whole of the walk, where he need do nothing about it.
    70	
