editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/compiled-prompt.md:2246:**Calendar.** No season, month or English weekday names; feet and yards. Day 58 Second-day, day 61 Fifth-day, day 64 First-day: Lira's three carters. About day 57: the confluence's stewards put the road meet back eight days for repairs to their hall (from day 63 to day 71; see owner flag 1). Day 66 Third-day: the note; "five drawers… shut" (the last two days before). Day 67: Withrow's colors sentence. **Day 68 Fifth-day: the small room**; Seln in the dark wing that night. Day 69 Sixth-day: the delegation leaves (Withrow and Bracken in the hired carriage, the coach, the program wagon; Rooke, the Stone, Lira, the Current third-year, Karis, Seln, Brom, Cael; Ephram stays). Day 70: the confluence at dusk; the card; Rooke's brief. **Day 71 First-day: the exhibition (afternoon); the production order served a quarter past two.** Day 72: finals; the corridor; the last evening at the rail. Days 73–74: home in rain. **Day 75 Fifth-day: the fourth sitting** (records produced; the one question). **Day 76 Sixth-day, second bell: the escort order at the gate**; noon refectory; Gault; the notebook; records hall; the Crown yard after dark. Bracken writes to the district seat on day 77 (the answer due about a week later). Brom's panel and the ruling share the year's last Fifth-day. The *fled* default would enter forty days after the fourth sitting's close (day 75) — the code's count, said by Seln.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/compiled-prompt.md:2269:- **Seln's case:** on the shelf above the copying table, untouched; the brass key in his waistcoat. Not mentioned aloud.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/compiled-prompt.md:2337:**Movement 4 CLOSED (2026-10-10).** Sol source-distance audit: 85 → r1 41 → r2 25 → r3 6, closed by ten Sol line fixes (eight chain fixes, two seams opened by cuts), applied by the coordinator. r2 canon checks PASS: Vastin's warning in ch27 is verbatim against B5 ch58:189 (*Because the people who want this to stop are not going to use official channels much longer.*) and Brom knows it via B5 ch59's long-table retelling; Seln's ch22 realisation that a return has nowhere to go past the last station stays at the M6 boundary. r2 fixes kept: Karis's notebook reply schedule; Bracken's "Leave me one more leaf…"; the "other gates" consequence after Vastin's warning. Cut in r2–r3 (later movements must not rely on them): Karis's forecast of the reply chain; the ch27 splinter, the form's blank line, the horse paragraph, Lira's written question; ch25 Withrow's public thanks and the Silver's "licences" reading; ch22's headings passage and the mother's-ledger detail. ~27,965 words. Overlap 0/7, gates 0, probe 1%/10%.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/compiled-prompt.md:2355:**Calendar.** No season or month names; feet and yards; Halcenvane weekdays. Day 77 Seventh-day: Seln at Bracken's counter; two favours; the drop; rain from the morning. Day 78 First-day: the cards read in the annex. Day 79 Second-day: the reach priced. Day 80 Third-day: the mould-room answer; Havel given the letter. Day 81 Fourth-day: the western answer; the grades; the catechism; the case carried to Cael at dusk; the cipher (five arrivals on day 85); the null report; the bridge chained at the third ring after the fourth bell, the town ferry tied up at noon; Havel's sixth entry that night. **Day 82 Fifth-day: the upper ferry; the cut (mid-morning); the reach and the unbinding; the fifth sitting (documentary) at the hour after noon; home over the bridge at dusk (water under the second ring).** Day 83 Sixth-day: schedule posted a day early (the five moved to day 88); fixity; Storm resettles (40 min; 15 min); the doorway (twelve seconds); Rooke. Day 84 Seventh-day: the idle state found by naming at dawn; Karis's curve; the district seat's answer. **Day 87 Third-day: the eleventh of Sowing — eighteen.** Day 88 Fourth-day: the annex (tomorrow at close). Brom's panel and the ruling share the year's last Fifth-day. The *fled* default would enter forty days after day 75.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/compiled-prompt.md:2366:- **Cael and the circle (Lira, Brom, Karis):** the woman on the Ostrand road and her craft as fought: points fixed against a surface; lines between them; points laid where a half beat says the body will go; nothing taken back; range costs a half-second stillness; a cage laid through a first point set against the body; release from inside unthreads it. The notice text. The fixity proposals; the doorway; the naming; Karis's curve *for now*. The team: six, no faces, no paper, no blades; a closed wagon with two rings. **Not reported** to the seat or registry (the four-minute decision); Withrow told; one line in her private book. The district seat's answer. Seln will open the case on day 88 in the reading room; nobody knows what is in it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/compiled-prompt.md:2367:- **Seln:** the paper traced (the second run; the fourteenth lot above the ruled line, a mark for a word); the four grades; has decided to open the case; **has not been told why Shadow was sealed and does not know a sealed thing exists**; **did not see the reach or the unbinding** (he was under the wagon in the gully; "I heard it"); knows the team broke off and the boy has ribs. **Does not know the mechanism.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/compiled-prompt.md:2368:- **Havel:** the seal absent from every registry of seals, recorded as a fact; nothing made of it; **six sheets, the last**. Learned nothing of the truth.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/compiled-prompt.md:2377:- **Seln:** two favours left (one never to be spent); the quick bag; the case **back on the shelf above the copying table**, unopened; the brass key; the null-report bundle with this week's duplicate; the floor schedule with the five on day 88.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/compiled-prompt.md:2391:- **Seln:** Bracken's narrow question; the favours; believes the boy; the case on the sill; "You're sure." / "No…"; the annex; "Five."; under the wagon; "Ribs?"; the cup turned; "It is a good room…"; the tenth bell.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/compiled-prompt.md:2409:- **Opened:** the case's opening (day 88, the reading room, five arrivals); Bracken's next letter; the wagon left in the gully (nobody will look); Withrow's private line; Lira's three *Not fought* on her program sheet; the doorway's line on the next leaf.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/compiled-prompt.md:2422:- (h) The birthday is in **the reading room** (tomorrow's room), so Seln's line about the room is about where he will open the case.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/compiled-prompt.md:2432:- **Ostrand bridge (flag):** five iron rings on the middle pier; shut to everybody at the third ring "since the year the middle arch went"; reopened under the second.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-24.md:87:She was at contact range, on a fast floor, against a man with nothing under his feet. The whole hall saw it at once. The noise on the south side stopped, not as a crowd's noise falls off but all together, as if a door had shut on it. Cael heard one person laugh on the north benches, high and astonished, and then nobody.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-24.md:131:Cael opened the notebook on his knee and wrote the fourth line under the other three. *A false quarter. SW, by the rope. Eight feet, crossways. Under the sawdust at dawn.*
books/book-06-the-compacts-hand/chapters/chapter-21.md:9:The records office opened at the first bell as it opened every day of the year, and the four of them were the first business of it, and Bracken had known they would be, and had set out four leaves of the correct form the night before, squared, with the inkstand where the light was good and a second pen laid beside the first in case a nib went. Cael counted the counter in on the way through the door because he had counted it in on his first morning at Halcenvane and intended to be consistent about it: the long oak top worn pale at the two places where hands rested; the pigeonholes behind, forty of them, alphabetical; the completed tray at the left and the pending at the right and the standing rule, posted in Bracken's hand for thirty years, that nothing crossed from right to left unverified. The morning light came in from the east window and lay along the counter in a bar, and the bar reached the completed tray at about the second bell, and Cael had watched it reach that tray perhaps two hundred times without ever once thinking he would remember it.
books/book-06-the-compacts-hand/chapters/chapter-21.md:87:The room heard the chair. Twenty fighters and an instructor turned, and the instructor stopped mid-sentence with the chalk still up, and Lira, at her place, said, "Thank you. It's been a good class and you're a good teacher," with complete courtesy and no explanation whatsoever, and picked up her kit, and walked the length of the table to the door, and opened it, and went out, and closed it behind her.
books/book-06-the-compacts-hand/chapters/chapter-21.md:129:At the gate: Withrow, who had timed her afternoon to be there without appearing to have timed anything — a chancellor crossing her own quadrangle at the hour her departing enrollees happened to reach the gate, with a folder under her arm that gave her a destination and that she never once opened.
books/book-06-the-compacts-hand/chapters/chapter-21.md:153:The road turned twice on the descent and gave the academy back twice, smaller each time: the lamps coming up along the covered walk at the first turn; at the second, only the Crown yard's western wall catching the last of the light above the river. Nobody in the cart said anything at either turn. Lira drove. Karis sat with the notebook shut. Brom sat with his back against the three boxes, which was where he sat.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/editions/eleven-v4-directors-cut/chapters/chapter-59.txt:175:The door was on the latch. Seln opened it, and stood aside.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/editions/eleven-v4-directors-cut/chapters/chapter-59.txt:191:Karis had seen it from the door. She had not gone to it at once; she had stood with her hands shut, as she must have stood in front of a locked press on a library's second floor, and then she had gone and opened it at the ribbon.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/editions/eleven-v4-directors-cut/chapters/chapter-59.txt:211:She did not shut it. She left it at the ribbon, as they had found it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/editions/eleven-v4-directors-cut/chapters/chapter-59.txt:247:Karis stopped with her toes against the stone and her notebook shut in both hands, and stepped over it without writing anything, which he had never seen her do at a door.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/editions/eleven-v4-directors-cut/chapters/chapter-59.txt:349:"Then it's right," said Karis. She opened her notebook with her pale fingers and wrote the figure down. "By definition. I shall have to think about that."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/editions/eleven-v4-directors-cut/chapters/chapter-59.txt:425:Cael looked at him doing it. He had lain under a cart last night and reckoned that there was nobody within three days who could carry a thing west, and he had been wrong by one night and a mule. He was glad that he had left a certain door shut.
