editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/review-editorial.stdout.log:5497:2. **The Storm notice.** Ch1: "The notice had found him on one knee on the stone, with a healer's fingers in his hand and eight thousand people looking down, and he had read it through twice there, before anybody strapped him." Ch4: each notice "had found him somewhere with nothing else to look at, a yard, a stair, a shut room, and the one from Norhold on one knee on a stone floor, with a healer holding his hand."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/review-editorial.stdout.log:5533:| 42–57 | ch7 | Redrafted whole. Changes, in order: <ul><li>The counsel: "I've looked tonight for the case where somebody turned these sections round to point at the man standing in the frame… This is new."</li><li>"Do you know the difference, in front of a seat, between a description and an evaluation?"</li><li>Bracken reads "flat"; the clerks' first-year joke ("the only page in the code nobody has ever had to stamp"); "imagined you" kept.</li><li>Withrow's morning after is rebuilt around the ferry, the guild master and the sealed file ("Kept, every page, perfectly safe, and nobody may open it"); "You can walk out of a town. You can't walk out of the post."; "Twice in my registry years I put my name to one. The first I'd sign again tomorrow… The second had a daughter."</li><li>The calendar: three silent marks read out by Karis ("The first. The eighth. The twenty-second."), with "in thirteen years I have never seen a seat take those three words back for anybody's lame horse".</li><li>The six slips are spoken as their words only, with one comment at the fifth.</li><li>The not-a-trick paragraph is now "Bracken would carry a paper like this. So would I… Look for the trick all night and you'll come up empty."</li><li>"the other choice has its own word in the docket, and the word is *fled*… I'll have bones on it in four days."</li><li>The stratum lead-in: "That clause is why you've never stood in a station since Denvash."</li><li>The note goes inside the front cover; the question mark: "She would answer it in her own time."</li><li>Seln's lamp: Cael "did not let himself guess what the man at the copying table was making".</li><li>Karis's instructions are cut to "Four days" and "Thank you for the tea".</li><li>The telling covers what moved the table, in a new order. Brom: "Then what's the answer for?" Cael's answer names the warden, provost and tournament himself; Lira: "And this time?… What if the people didn't fail this time?"; Lira leaves without the "Bed" line; Brom's second "Corridor." comes at the door.</li><li>Pole frame: "The entry was finished before the pen touched paper."</li><li>The prolepsis is trimmed to "It looked like the truth, because, as far as he could see from that window, it was."</li><li>The lamps go out by the hall's own count (the counter pair, the table's pairs from the far end, the press lamp last).</li></ul> |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/review-editorial.stdout.log:5759:editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-39.md:143:"I can tell you when the policy began, near enough, and that it was a policy, and that it's been kept since by forms. I can tell you that the oldest thing it did was shut a door the old way had left open, and take the name off the people who'd used it. I can't tell you what the old word was for, before. I can't tell you what the reading is, underneath the function, or how old, or how it came to be there to have a race cut beside it. Nothing in that case reaches down that far, not a line." She put the slip on top of the first one. "We've explained the middle of the story. Not the beginning. Entered as a limit."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/review-editorial.stdout.log:5822:editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/state/movement-009/review-cold.md:55:| Progression payoff | 8 | 55: the touch earned by Karis's burned card and the shut hall; 56: FRAGMENT ACQUIRED — "Stability: provisional"; 56: "He called for the landing beat, and the wrong thing answered." | Effort visibly changes capability (the air-read) and consequence (the stumble, the Wind answering from "the wrong side of him" for weeks). One small dissonance: the notice says *Tier equivalent: Gold* for a lane the text calls fifteen feet, a third as deep, "nothing a Storm instructor would have let a first-year walk." A cold reader can reconcile it (the source's tier, not the product's) but the text doesn't help. | Medium-high |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/review-editorial.stdout.log:5842:editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-37.md-133-Cael went on, because there was nothing else to do. He told the rule counted on five fingers against Brom's coat: earnest, a man spending everything he had in the light and meaning every word; his, begun by him, before Cael knew there was anything to begin; close, one flight; his work, the wing's officer doing the wing's work; and awake, the little finger. He told how he had not done it the way he did a burst, all at once before thinking could catch up, but slowly, on purpose, on the cold stone, knowing exactly what he did and to whom. And the quiet coming down over him like a heavy door swung shut, the stair's sounds gone, the light gone flat, and three seconds or four of the night going on above him without him in it. And then the notice.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/review-editorial.stdout.log:5945:editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/STATE_LEDGER.md-860-- **Wind:** the ceiling is restated at **six** free on sprung oak (the seventh billed to tomorrow, the eighth to the day after); the landing beat is unshortened. The **aborted burst** was shut mid-payment once and cannot be repeated ("one point isn't a line"). It is a Wind event, not a fragment and not a technique.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/review-editorial.stdout.log:6004:   243	Karis had begun putting the case back in its order and did not raise her head. Brom was standing with his good hand on the rail of the chair Vastin had left, as though it might still hold some of the warmth.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/review-editorial.stdout.log:6016:   255	At the fourth station, a day upriver from Ostrand, the keeper had walked him through the frame room as keepers always did, proud of his brass, and at the end of it had opened a long drawer under the counter to show him the station's own sheets for the year. A keeper kept his sheets as a miller kept his tallies. They were the station's private record of what its frame had read on each child, before any clerk of entry had touched it, and this keeper wrote a good hand and wanted it seen.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/review-editorial.stdout.log:6100:   203	"One." Karis looked at him. "It opens on one day, the day of the ruling, and stays open until the revocation takes effect, and then it shuts. And it only opens at all if we lose. If the seat rules for the house, there's no door, because there's nothing to resign from." She sat back. "Until that day there's only the corridor: every sitting attended, every form filed on time, every bout in wing three at the band, and every first-year at that counter handing in a certificate, and you standing behind her in the queue with your face doing nothing." She was quiet a moment. "Perfectly, until the ruling. If we put one foot wrong before it, the door we'd use afterward turns into the word on four files."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/review-editorial.stdout.log:6126:   229	She had the bench by the rail, with Rooke's red drill-book on her knee for something to hold and her right foot out straight on the boards. Karis had chalk and her grey notebook and her coat buttoned right for once. Brom had gone up the gallery stair and drawn every shutter down the length of the north wall, as Lira had drawn them on the first honest floor of the year. Now he stood in the hall's great doorway, with one of the two tall doors standing open a hand's breadth onto the dark of the passage and his right hand on its edge.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/review-editorial.stdout.log:6149:   167	The five of them sat in the reading room under the shaded lamp, with the case on its shelf between the grey boxes and the lamp in the window turned up as high as every night, and Karis laid it out for them on the bare cloth in the order she had found it. She had the code's second volume open on the left and the old enrollment book open on the right, and a single sheet of her own between them with five lines on it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/review-editorial.stdout.log:6177:    41	*They did this to me the other way — built the ladder to my height and called it fairness.* He had the letter by heart; it lived inside the back board of Hesk's book, in the satchel across his chest. He had never told Karis its words. She had come to the same sentence from the far side of a case.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/review-editorial.stdout.log:6191:    55	"The leaf says the function is appended to the reading and advises what's entered. It doesn't say what happens when the reading gives it nothing to advise, and nothing else in the case says it in words." She looked at Cael. "But your file says it. The petition put it in schedule two by its full title, on the first night of the year, and you read it. *Suppression-Advisory Watch, Priority Level 4.*"
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/review-editorial.stdout.log:6234:+Interest caught immediately in chapter 35's first line, because the new Anchor-adjacent perception has stopped asking and Cael does not trust the silence. It tightened when the case came off the shelf and fully caught at the river-town father's letter: that letter turns institutional harm from a theory into one child asking her father what she is. The strongest emotional material belongs to Seln—especially Lira asking what it cost him to remain pleasant, Cael revealing the Shadow fragment, and Seln realizing, “You kept my file too, then.” Vastin's refusal to join the circle is the right payoff because it preserves both his integrity and his independence.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/review-editorial.stdout.log:6271:+- **Plan adherence:** The case arrives in ordered objects; Karis supplies four findings and a limit; the clean door is found; Anchor practice stays non-deploying; the borrowed office and three refusals land; the final Vastin window pays the planted northern file. The quiet movement still has one embodied learning encounter.
