editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-005/recheck-r1.stdout.log:4675:**Movement 4 CLOSED (2026-10-10).** Sol source-distance audit: 85 → r1 41 → r2 25 → r3 6, closed by ten Sol line fixes (eight chain fixes, two seams opened by cuts), applied by the coordinator. r2 canon checks PASS: Vastin's warning in ch27 is verbatim against B5 ch58:189 (*Because the people who want this to stop are not going to use official channels much longer.*) and Brom knows it via B5 ch59's long-table retelling; Seln's ch22 realisation that a return has nowhere to go past the last station stays at the M6 boundary. r2 fixes kept: Karis's notebook reply schedule; Bracken's "Leave me one more leaf…"; the "other gates" consequence after Vastin's warning. Cut in r2–r3 (later movements must not rely on them): Karis's forecast of the reply chain; the ch27 splinter, the form's blank line, the horse paragraph, Lira's written question; ch25 Withrow's public thanks and the Silver's "licences" reading; ch22's headings passage and the mother's-ledger detail. ~27,965 words. Overlap 0/7, gates 0, probe 1%/10%.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-005/recheck-r1.stdout.log:4693:**Calendar.** No season or month names; feet and yards; Halcenvane weekdays. Day 77 Seventh-day: Seln at Bracken's counter; two favours; the drop; rain from the morning. Day 78 First-day: the cards read in the annex. Day 79 Second-day: the reach priced. Day 80 Third-day: the mould-room answer; Havel given the letter. Day 81 Fourth-day: the western answer; the grades; the catechism; the case carried to Cael at dusk; the cipher (five arrivals on day 85); the null report; the bridge chained at the third ring after the fourth bell, the town ferry tied up at noon; Havel's sixth entry that night. **Day 82 Fifth-day: the upper ferry; the cut (mid-morning); the reach and the unbinding; the fifth sitting (documentary) at the hour after noon; home over the bridge at dusk (water under the second ring).** Day 83 Sixth-day: schedule posted a day early (the five moved to day 88); fixity; Storm resettles (40 min; 15 min); the doorway (twelve seconds); Rooke. Day 84 Seventh-day: the idle state found by naming at dawn; Karis's curve; the district seat's answer. **Day 87 Third-day: the eleventh of Sowing — eighteen.** Day 88 Fourth-day: the annex (tomorrow at close). Brom's panel and the ruling share the year's last Fifth-day. The *fled* default would enter forty days after day 75.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-005/recheck-r1.stdout.log:4704:- **Cael and the circle (Lira, Brom, Karis):** the woman on the Ostrand road and her craft as fought: points fixed against a surface; lines between them; points laid where a half beat says the body will go; nothing taken back; range costs a half-second stillness; a cage laid through a first point set against the body; release from inside unthreads it. The notice text. The fixity proposals; the doorway; the naming; Karis's curve *for now*. The team: six, no faces, no paper, no blades; a closed wagon with two rings. **Not reported** to the seat or registry (the four-minute decision); Withrow told; one line in her private book. The district seat's answer. Seln will open the case on day 88 in the reading room; nobody knows what is in it.
