editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-005/recheck-r1.stdout.log:7052:editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/state/completion/listening-proof.md:36:  cases use either italics (the Log, the documents, reported speech) or single quotes (ch57 Brom repeating Rooke; ch58
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-005/recheck-r1.stdout.log:7080:editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/state/movement-006/review-editorial-prompt.md:777:After supper he read the floor allocations on the covered walk's board, which he had written himself, as if they were news, and went up the staff stair at the pace of a man going to bed. There was nothing for the small case tonight. He sat on the bed's edge for a while, listening to the river under the bluff, and then he put the lamp out.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-005/recheck-r1.stdout.log:7093:editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/state/movement-006/recheck-r1.md:62:Reproduced (see §3): mean 13.23 → **13.61** (aim ≈13.6); ≥40-word share 4.4% → **3.7%** (aim ≤4.0%); words/scene 1,017.8 (850–1,050); prose words 31,551; wc 31,621 (30,500–33,000). I read every join in the diff: all are narration; none touches dialogue, a Log line, a landing beat or protected text. The long minute (ch42 lines 171–203) and both semifinal exchange sequences are byte-identical to pre-repair. Splits are at a natural turn in every case I checked (e.g. ch38 line 25, ch39 line 43, ch42 line 5, ch44 line 63).
