editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-005/recheck-r1.stdout.log:8733:-It was a good rubbing. It was also a good seal. That was the first thing he noticed and the thing he went on noticing all afternoon: whoever had cut the die had cut it properly. The river ran the right way. The scale's beam was level. The beading round the rim was even and close, and in the beading, at the bottom, where every registry die carried its cutter's number, there were four small figures that the pencil had picked out faintly, as a pencil does when it passes over something raised. He took the reading glass out of his kit and bent over them until he was sure of all four.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-005/recheck-r1.stdout.log:8734:+It was a good rubbing, and it was also a good seal. That was the first thing he noticed and the thing he went on noticing all afternoon: whoever had cut the die had cut it properly. The river ran the right way; the scale's beam was level. The beading round the rim was even and close, and in the beading, at the bottom, where every registry die carried its cutter's number, there were four small figures that the pencil had picked out faintly, as a pencil does when it passes over something raised. He took the reading glass out of his kit and bent over them until he was sure of all four.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-005/recheck-r1.stdout.log:8757:-*The seal on the instrument constituting the facilities office named in the order presented at Halcenvane, and on the order itself (registrar's rubbing): absent from the district's impression book; absent from the registry's schedule of seals of office, this year's and last; its rim number absent from the cutters' issue ledger, which runs without a line between the numbers on either side of it. Checked three ways. Absent from every registry of seals.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-005/recheck-r1.stdout.log:8758:+*The seal on the instrument constituting the facilities office named in the order presented at Halcenvane, and on the order itself (registrar's rubbing): absent from the district's impression book; absent from the registry's schedule of seals of office, this year's and last; its rim number absent from the cutters' issue ledger, where the numbers one below it and one above it stand on consecutive lines with no line for it between. Checked three ways. Absent from every registry of seals.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-005/recheck-r1.stdout.log:8791:-Something large in him lifted its head. He had never found a better way to put it, though Karis had asked him for one more than once: a great slow weight that had lain quiet since the dawn on the second floor, raising itself to look at whatever had just come into the house. His ears closed and opened. The air in the room changed its weight, not much, the way the air changes before thunder. On the sill, in the corner where the porter's girl never quite reached with her cloth, the little drift of grey dust woke up and began to run, slowly, in a thin stream along the edge of the wood, toward the window frame.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-005/recheck-r1.stdout.log:8795:+Then his ears closed and opened, and he knew. Something large in him had lifted its head: the great slow weight that had lain quiet since the dawn on the second floor, raising itself to look at whatever had just come into the house. The air in the room changed its weight, not much, the way air does before thunder.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-005/recheck-r1.stdout.log:8815:-It was made of brown leather, the good thick kind that Hesk bought for instrument cases and would not use for anything that did not deserve it. It was plain. It had a flap that came down over the front and a strap long enough to go across a man's body and rest on the opposite hip, so that it would not swing when he walked, or ran. The buckle on the strap was brass, and it was not a bought buckle. Cael knew it at once. He had watched Hesk file buckles at the long bench since he was small enough to sleep in the shavings under it, and this one had Hesk's file marks on the inside of the tongue where nobody would see them, and a little bevel on the frame that Hesk put on everything he made so that it would not catch on cloth.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-005/recheck-r1.stdout.log:8816:+He did not look at the outside of it first. He opened the flap and put his hand in, the way he would have put his hand into any bag Hesk had made, to find out what it was for, and against the back his fingers found a pocket stitched flat and close in Hesk's waxed thread.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-005/recheck-r1.stdout.log:8824:+Only then did Cael look at the rest. The flap came down over everything. The strap was long enough to cross a man's body and ride on the opposite hip, so that the bag would sit still when he walked and not swing when he ran. And the buckle was not a bought buckle. Hesk's file marks were on the inside of the tongue, where only somebody who had slept in the shavings under that bench would think to look, and the frame had the little bevel Hesk put on everything he made so that it would not catch on cloth. He ran his thumb over the bevel. The leather round it was the heavy brown kind Hesk kept for instrument cases and would not waste on anything that did not deserve it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-005/recheck-r1.stdout.log:8984:- **Seln's case:** on the shelf above the copying table, untouched; the brass key in his waistcoat. Not mentioned aloud.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-005/recheck-r1.stdout.log:9052:**Movement 4 CLOSED (2026-10-10).** Sol source-distance audit: 85 → r1 41 → r2 25 → r3 6, closed by ten Sol line fixes (eight chain fixes, two seams opened by cuts), applied by the coordinator. r2 canon checks PASS: Vastin's warning in ch27 is verbatim against B5 ch58:189 (*Because the people who want this to stop are not going to use official channels much longer.*) and Brom knows it via B5 ch59's long-table retelling; Seln's ch22 realisation that a return has nowhere to go past the last station stays at the M6 boundary. r2 fixes kept: Karis's notebook reply schedule; Bracken's "Leave me one more leaf…"; the "other gates" consequence after Vastin's warning. Cut in r2–r3 (later movements must not rely on them): Karis's forecast of the reply chain; the ch27 splinter, the form's blank line, the horse paragraph, Lira's written question; ch25 Withrow's public thanks and the Silver's "licences" reading; ch22's headings passage and the mother's-ledger detail. ~27,965 words. Overlap 0/7, gates 0, probe 1%/10%.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-005/recheck-r1.stdout.log:9070:**Calendar.** No season or month names; feet and yards; Halcenvane weekdays. Day 77 Seventh-day: Seln at Bracken's counter; two favours; the drop; rain from the morning. Day 78 First-day: the cards read in the annex. Day 79 Second-day: the reach priced. Day 80 Third-day: the mould-room answer; Havel given the letter. Day 81 Fourth-day: the western answer; the grades; the catechism; the case carried to Cael at dusk; the cipher (five arrivals on day 85); the null report; the bridge chained at the third ring after the fourth bell, the town ferry tied up at noon; Havel's sixth entry that night. **Day 82 Fifth-day: the upper ferry; the cut (mid-morning); the reach and the unbinding; the fifth sitting (documentary) at the hour after noon; home over the bridge at dusk (water under the second ring).** Day 83 Sixth-day: schedule posted a day early (the five moved to day 88); fixity; Storm resettles (40 min; 15 min); the doorway (twelve seconds); Rooke. Day 84 Seventh-day: the idle state found by naming at dawn; Karis's curve; the district seat's answer. **Day 87 Third-day: the eleventh of Sowing — eighteen.** Day 88 Fourth-day: the annex (tomorrow at close). Brom's panel and the ruling share the year's last Fifth-day. The *fled* default would enter forty days after day 75.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-005/recheck-r1.stdout.log:9081:- **Cael and the circle (Lira, Brom, Karis):** the woman on the Ostrand road and her craft as fought: points fixed against a surface; lines between them; points laid where a half beat says the body will go; nothing taken back; range costs a half-second stillness; a cage laid through a first point set against the body; release from inside unthreads it. The notice text. The fixity proposals; the doorway; the naming; Karis's curve *for now*. The team: six, no faces, no paper, no blades; a closed wagon with two rings. **Not reported** to the seat or registry (the four-minute decision); Withrow told; one line in her private book. The district seat's answer. Seln will open the case on day 88 in the reading room; nobody knows what is in it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-005/recheck-r1.stdout.log:9082:- **Seln:** the paper traced (the second run; the fourteenth lot above the ruled line, a mark for a word); the four grades; has decided to open the case; **has not been told why Shadow was sealed and does not know a sealed thing exists**; **did not see the reach or the unbinding** (he was under the wagon in the gully; "I heard it"); knows the team broke off and the boy has ribs. **Does not know the mechanism.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-005/recheck-r1.stdout.log:9083:- **Havel:** the seal absent from every registry of seals, recorded as a fact; nothing made of it; **six sheets, the last**. Learned nothing of the truth.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-005/recheck-r1.stdout.log:9092:- **Seln:** two favours left (one never to be spent); the quick bag; the case **back on the shelf above the copying table**, unopened; the brass key; the null-report bundle with this week's duplicate; the floor schedule with the five on day 88.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-005/recheck-r1.stdout.log:9106:- **Seln:** Bracken's narrow question; the favours; believes the boy; the case on the sill; "You're sure." / "No…"; the annex; "Five."; under the wagon; "Ribs?"; the cup turned; "It is a good room…"; the tenth bell.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-005/recheck-r1.stdout.log:9124:- **Opened:** the case's opening (day 88, the reading room, five arrivals); Bracken's next letter; the wagon left in the gully (nobody will look); Withrow's private line; Lira's three *Not fought* on her program sheet; the doorway's line on the next leaf.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-005/recheck-r1.stdout.log:9137:- (h) The birthday is in **the reading room** (tomorrow's room), so Seln's line about the room is about where he will open the case.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-005/recheck-r1.stdout.log:9147:- **Ostrand bridge (flag):** five iron rings on the middle pier; shut to everybody at the third ring "since the year the middle arch went"; reopened under the second.
