editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/recheck-r2.stdout.log:1430:| 25 | The Rail | 4,682 | 6 | Seln's head turns first; **the production order** — an officer in grey with a case held before him, the clerk carrying nothing; **fifty-one seconds** counted along the north benches, the hall turning from the Current girl's bout; *the complete records of evaluation-linked floor work of the enrollee of record, Caelen Hesk-ward*; Bracken reads it standing, signs, takes the duplicate; **Withrow thanks the officer by full grade** to four rows. Lawful in every line; "The hour is not in the order." **The hall's regard adjusting**: applause taken back to be weighed; the steward; two correspondents out. Lira at the rope: "They waited… Till I'd lost well"; the boy's card and his mother. Supper: **Seln's clerk** on the south benches since the first bell, out at the second touch, back with the officer nineteen minutes later; "They waited for the hall"; Withrow: bind the records "in the house's own boards… they may look at it handsomely." **LIRA cutaway (~1,770), day 72**: the corridor of trestles; the Silver — "go on your fifth"; "Because you'd asked"; the town and its licences; the finals' politeness. Evening rail: the steward's sheet *for your file*; the ladder counted rung by rung (Iron Rank One; 27 in the red book; one point under a hall's seal; the Stone; Zerin's *Silver bracket. Next cycle.*; the corridor); four nights since the dairy; no Silver card past the stamps. Cael with the order's duplicate. **"One of these is the best night of my life." / "Noted."** The folds won't lie the same way twice; it will go in the box. Home in rain; the watcher looks at the colors trunk; log: *They can't touch the paper. The paper's honest. So they choose the hour.* |
