editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/recheck-r2.stdout.log:6528:editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md-94-- The Velmere letters (two more arrive in this book; the second stays unopened).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/recheck-r2.stdout.log:6532:editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md-98-- Seln's case (opened M6).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/recheck-r2.stdout.log:6579:editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md-462-**Calendar.** No season, month or English weekday names. Day 9 Second-day: drafting begins (four days to bones). Day 12 Fifth-day: bones. Day 13 night: the integrity section. Day 16: the counter. Two nights of Bracken's reading; the first rain; the weighing. **Day 19, Fifth-day: the answer goes down, three days inside the time** (due day 22). **Day 23: the seat's notice. Day 25, Fourth-day: Jent's conference; Withrow's office that evening.** Day 26 Fifth-day: board line; wing three. Day 27: the coats placed; the honest floor. **Day 30, Second-day: Lira's trial.** Day 31: the district docket's confirmation and the Velmere letter; opened the third evening (day 33). Day 35: Karis's budget; the frames days 35–38. Day 39: the annex convening. **Day 40, Fifth-day (the year's sixth): the first sitting.** **Day 42, Seventh-day: the month's close.** Lira's first meet off the hill is about four weeks away (Rooke's board). Brom's panel and the ruling share the year's last Fifth-day.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/recheck-r2.stdout.log:6635:editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md-550-- **Havel at Ostrand:** the inn by the bridge; junior chair, rotation "the seat's Fifth-days, until relieved"; the senior chair district grade; the five sheets stay at the inn on sitting days; "told, once, in a room with the door shut, that the mark was not his clearance".
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/recheck-r2.stdout.log:6636:editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md-551-- **Withrow:** the charter folder in the locked case under the framed charter, key on her chain; the two old adverse notes (a fire-watch quarter; a year's declarations unindexed) with remedies and clearances.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/recheck-r2.stdout.log:6648:editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md-563-- THE VELMERE LETTER (day 45) stays SEALED: Brom pockets it unopened (left pocket), carried visibly through ch18–20; it is BOOK_MAP §4e #10's unopened letter for M7. The table keeps its agreement not to ask.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/recheck-r2.stdout.log:6649:editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md:564:- New canon: a gallery over wing three's west door; Rooke shuts the program floor to observers from day 46 (and chains the gallery stair before the visitors); a burst spent small can pass for a step; the Ostrand fee office seals archive requests and queries standing; the gate lodge's road column "since the year of the thieves"; under lamps the lane's dust casts a shadow Lira learns to read; Hesk's surveyor's-level story (no lesson drawn aloud); Cael writes back to Hesk by Bracken's pouch (Seln's advice); Gault's minute line on the four observers; Brom and Ephram at the old frames without speaking; at the ferry one watcher looks at the house's document cases, not at Cael; Vastin strikes a refusal of his own in the old form and rewrites it with a citation.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/recheck-r2.stdout.log:6679:editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md-594-- **Hesk's book:** the column now has lines under Lira (the gallery log; the floor shut; "she says it's fine"; the file read *for completeness*, per her request on day 49), Brom (the Velmere letter) and Karis (the fee office's query; the assistant on the covered walk); **his own name still blank**. Log entries: the weekly question; Withrow's mercy; the order wrong; the dullest hour; the oak; Daeva filed; the line he can't find; the honest floor; counting doors.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/recheck-r2.stdout.log:6684:editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md-617-- **Ephram:** the confiscated woodcut; "You're a case"; the chart that agrees; the captain's note.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/recheck-r2.stdout.log:6728:editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md-661-- **Rooke:** business in the town on Third-day evenings; the sentence to the correspondent; the program floor closed to observers from day 46 (shutters, chain and padlock, card *PROGRAM FLOOR CLOSED TO OBSERVERS. BY ORDER.*), the visitors' ledger kept with *none*.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/recheck-r2.stdout.log:6748:editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md-694-**Calendar.** No season, month or English weekday names; feet and yards. Day 58 Second-day, day 61 Fifth-day, day 64 First-day: Lira's three carters. About day 57: the confluence's stewards put the road meet back eight days for repairs to their hall (from day 63 to day 71; see owner flag 1). Day 66 Third-day: the note; "five drawers… shut" (the last two days before). Day 67: Withrow's colors sentence. **Day 68 Fifth-day: the small room**; Seln in the dark wing that night. Day 69 Sixth-day: the delegation leaves (Withrow and Bracken in the hired carriage, the coach, the program wagon; Rooke, the Stone, Lira, the Current third-year, Karis, Seln, Brom, Cael; Ephram stays). Day 70: the confluence at dusk; the card; Rooke's brief. **Day 71 First-day: the exhibition (afternoon); the production order served a quarter past two.** Day 72: finals; the corridor; the last evening at the rail. Days 73–74: home in rain. **Day 75 Fifth-day: the fourth sitting** (records produced; the one question). **Day 76 Sixth-day, second bell: the escort order at the gate**; noon refectory; Gault; the notebook; records hall; the Crown yard after dark. Bracken writes to the district seat on day 77 (the answer due about a week later). Brom's panel and the ruling share the year's last Fifth-day. The *fled* default would enter forty days after the fourth sitting's close (day 75) — the code's count, said by Seln.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/recheck-r2.stdout.log:6813:editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md-28-**Karis knows:** the fielding clause (sixth part, subsection four; copied and banked on the twelfth of the new month: "Interesting." / "It's banked."); its forty-year history (the placement scandal) and that the charter predates the last registry standardization (both the source's, to be taught in M1); the retired word's passage: read, in her Greyvane notebooks, identified to the directive's terminology article, voiced once at Halcenvane (B4 ch50, the word lower-case in her mouth, one factual clause) and closed as *Why retire a working method?*; the notebooks went by hand-cart (four loads) to the named top-floor room on the night of the twenty-seventh, Bracken's card in ninety seconds, and the archive sweep of the tenth found carrel eleven *nil*. She will find the bracket rule (*no tier seeding applicable … demonstration-exhibition provisions*) on the second day of drafting. She saw a slip burned on the common-room coals and asked nothing. She keeps the marbled watcher log. [B4-reconciled 2026-10-05]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/recheck-r2.stdout.log:6824:editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md-39-- **Enrollment:** the demonstration provision of the assay clause, with one semester stamp, renewed (Bracken's line in the enrollment book on the twenty-second of Reaping; Gault's note of the twentieth: growth confirmed in five, the plate flat; the record keeps five capabilities, two of them public). Gault is the evaluator of record. Next term's sitting is already ruled on his calendar, the provision's half-yearly evaluation: *Panel of record: Gault, with two. Measured against: baseline (entry), and the note of the twentieth of Reaping.*; same instruments, checked on Fourth-days; the frame to get a new second notch. So the mill-town session (M2) is the provision's SECOND evaluation, not its third (§12 C8). The panel "travels" (a seals case with a handle) is the source's, to be staged in M1. [B4-reconciled 2026-10-05]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/recheck-r2.stdout.log:6826:editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md:41:- **Documents:** three copies and a certified transcription of the tournament charter (Karis read it on the afternoon of Withrow's address; Withrow: posted before selection); Bracken's certified season sheets (about three hundred, across the recess); Karis's grey notebook (the clause and *Interesting.*; Ember's three words) and her marbled watcher log; Rooke's profiles table (forty-one names); Seln's cipher page in the small case (the quarterly is gone down the fish steps); Vastin's file note in the Compact's folder (nobody on the bluff has seen it) and his four-sentence private letter to Bracken praising the enrollment index (sent by the morning post; whether Bracken has shown it to anyone is open); and, from Movement 2, the Standard's public documentation (forty pages) and the examiner's annotated manual. [B4-reconciled 2026-10-05]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/recheck-r2.stdout.log:6832:editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md-47-| 1 | Wind-adjacent | Lira | Working ceiling **six bursts free on the sprung oak** (stone fewer; the seventh billed to the next morning, the eighth to the morning after), measured by the panel on the twentieth; unchanged all recess ("the cost structure is the thing to work on"). Landing beat locked and unshortened (ch62: "Three years of trying to trim it"; B5's inventories count four, N9). The quarter-burst, shut mid-payment once: "one point isn't a line", not in the column. Public at documented rate [B4-reconciled 2026-10-05] |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/recheck-r2.stdout.log:6844:editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md:72:| Vastin | One interview (B4 ch56: eleven questions in a twelve-by-fourteen room, the twelfth not asked); civil baseline; nothing warmer or colder yet. On the evaluation morning he looked once at the failing frame and not again at Cael that whole morning. He has decided that if the question ever becomes properly his he will ask it "in a room with the door shut and tell the boy first." [B4-reconciled 2026-10-05] |
