editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/recheck-r2.stdout.log:7726:editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-05.md-45-He unlocked the case with a key from his watch-chain and took out a form first, a single printed sheet with two ruled lines at its foot. Cael had never seen its like. It was headed *Acknowledgment of Joint Service*, and under the heading there was a paragraph of small type, and under that, two lines.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/recheck-r2.stdout.log:7730:editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-13.md-21-She took out her notebook and turned it over, and opened it from the back, where the six slips from the long table lived in their pocket behind the last leaf with Brom's two dates beside them. On the inside of the back board she wrote the request's number and *Greyvane: the founders' hands*, and under it she ruled three short lines and left them empty.
