editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/recheck-r2.stdout.log:10433:editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-002/review-editorial.md-526-- **ch12:243–265.** The Velmere letter came on day 31. "Two days later it was still on his table", "one more night" and "On the third evening he opened it" can be heard as the 34th. Lira's leg is still up on Rooke's stool at that supper, which is days 31–32. "The next evening" for "Two days later" lands the opening on the 33rd, as the author's ledger has it.
