editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/recheck-r2.stdout.log:11189:editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/source-tracking.stdout.log-2113-    33	Senior evaluator of record, in the registry's grey, files squared on the seat's lap-desk at angles that had not varied by a degree since the first counter she had ever read his case across — the woman who had read that case at the counter of his life and had been, in every recorded act since, exactly correct. She had come in with the working morning's traffic rather than with the officers, carrying her own files, and had set them down and squared them, and had spent the four minutes before the opening reading the topmost one with the specific attention of a person who has read it three times already and intends to read it a fourth.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/recheck-r2.stdout.log:11191:editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/source-tracking.stdout.log:2115:    35	Empaneled. The clerk read the empanelment into the minute: *the evaluation seat constituted, the district's senior evaluator presiding, scope per the code's institutional provisions.* Ilsev inclined her head to the seal at the exact depth the registry taught, and opened the first of her files, and the room proceeded, and Cael sat with the reading the sight of her produced, which was not comfort and was not its opposite.
