editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/recheck-r2.stdout.log:12127:editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:18:| 23 | Colors | 4,322 | 5 | Day 69 dawn: the colors out of their cedar trunk, the creased pennant; Bracken's travel sheet ("Attendance. Again."). Day 67 flashback: Bracken's question; **Withrow's one sentence** ("The house sends its fighters in its own colors, Registrar, or it does not send them, and nobody at Ostrand has yet asked me to stop sending them."). The road north: Karis changing one word on a card four times (not shown to Cael); Seln without his case; **Rooke at the waystation trough** — the registry reads meet records; "The program is getting things written down where nobody can rub them off"; Cael hears his own pole in it, and every rung on this side of the stamps. The confluence (callback to B5): the innkeeper's framed ruling; Withrow's tea and "careful in writing for sixty days". **The card**: one line on the non-qualifying year's lighter card; Rooke's filing under the host's exhibition provision (stated once); the Silver's acceptance on a barge manifest, *Yes. Glad to.*; Silver eleven years, never asked by an Iron. The river apron at night: Lira frightened "of being a good loss"; "Watch my feet." **Rooke's brief** in bread: courses under courses; four counts — "Before four it's a promise. After four it's a floor."; lose the first slowly, one burst; the second is the exam; the Stone: "Watch his knees." Lira: "growth". **Dawn**: Rooke walks the floor (slower: the stewards' letter said *repairs*); Cael charts **no light, no rebound, a quiet side that pulls**, leaves a fourth line blank (the south-west corner under sawdust). Breakfast: Brom's bowl; **"He calls it honesty. I'm going to call it the ropes."** |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/recheck-r2.stdout.log:12129:editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:20:| 25 | The Rail | 4,682 | 6 | Seln's head turns first; **the production order** — an officer in grey with a case held before him, the clerk carrying nothing; **fifty-one seconds** counted along the north benches, the hall turning from the Current girl's bout; *the complete records of evaluation-linked floor work of the enrollee of record, Caelen Hesk-ward*; Bracken reads it standing, signs, takes the duplicate; **Withrow thanks the officer by full grade** to four rows. Lawful in every line; "The hour is not in the order." **The hall's regard adjusting**: applause taken back to be weighed; the steward; two correspondents out. Lira at the rope: "They waited… Till I'd lost well"; the boy's card and his mother. Supper: **Seln's clerk** on the south benches since the first bell, out at the second touch, back with the officer nineteen minutes later; "They waited for the hall"; Withrow: bind the records "in the house's own boards… they may look at it handsomely." **LIRA cutaway (~1,770), day 72**: the corridor of trestles; the Silver — "go on your fifth"; "Because you'd asked"; the town and its licences; the finals' politeness. Evening rail: the steward's sheet *for your file*; the ladder counted rung by rung (Iron Rank One; 27 in the red book; one point under a hall's seal; the Stone; Zerin's *Silver bracket. Next cycle.*; the corridor); four nights since the dairy; no Silver card past the stamps. Cael with the order's duplicate. **"One of these is the best night of my life." / "Noted."** The folds won't lie the same way twice; it will go in the box. Home in rain; the watcher looks at the colors trunk; log: *They can't touch the paper. The paper's honest. So they choose the hour.* |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/recheck-r2.stdout.log:12130:editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:21:| 26 | One Question | 4,770 | 5 | Flashback: **the assistant finds a struck heading** in the code's index — *Of the seat's hearing, and who may be heard*; para 1, a question through counsel; **para 2, the advocate heard at the close by the seat's leave** (no recorded use); a hundred and forty years; the counsel: "Old law is an old floor… one question… And the second paragraph we leave exactly where it is… Until the end." (M8 setup, light.) **Day 75:** the side-door officer enters Karis as *Advocate of record for the respondent, under the hearing provision*. Lot seventeen. **The records produced in the house's boards**; Jent: never seen a production order answered in boards. **The interrogatory**: the hood permits one question; the counsel speaks the card from memory; Ilsev looks up and stays up; not one pencil moves; Havel writes the time; **"None, Advocate. The petition doesn't turn on evidence. It turns on discretion."** Cael's dairy notes: every receipt is evidence — *He had brought receipts to a room that did not take them.* Steps: "Did you hear what he called me?"; the counsel: "Keep the other paragraph… In your pocket, not your mouth."; Jent: "A good question, Advocate. I'd have asked it myself, in your chair."; Karis: "He wasn't even careful." The card with question and answer goes inside her notebook's front cover. The counsel stays the night. **Day 76, the gate:** the lodge-man shuts his road window; the boy runs; Cael behind the old bell-frame on the gatehouse; the court (the level flags round the capped well); **pass one** (three paces, nothing). Withrow reads the lodge board (*ANYTHING SEALED — FETCH THE REGISTRAR*); "My lodge-man… has never once heard one read"; **the order read aloud**, 81 words with its heading *In the matter of Caelen Hesk-ward.*; **Bracken's minute and forty** (paper, deckle, glass, then his thumb on the impression with eyes shut); **pass two** (the one level patch); south-mill paper, registry die, an office he has never met in thirteen years; "Facilities"; "my book has a column for the office that issues… I can't write four riders in it." |
