editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-31.md:55:The book came down from the eleventh shelf of the eastern gallery, on the two hundred and eighty-eighth day, in a girl's right hand.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-31.md:125:"Twenty-three." Karis had that figure now. The last of the Ring's eleven had been laid that morning, and she had gone down all fifty-two with her pencil upright. "Seven kinds bear. Eleven are nothing at all. And there are twenty-three which are carried; and those, it appears, are what a word is spelled in."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-31.md:265:Brom paid at the half-door in the morning, on the two hundred and eighty-ninth day, and the woman swept two marks off her ledge with the side of her hand.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-31.md:267:"A hundred and thirty-four," he said, to the purse.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-33.md:81:"I have three days, and I have fourteen letters. If a paper is served on me tomorrow, at a registry's own yard door, then four people have carried fifty-two sheets up that hill for a week to no purpose, and a man below will never be told why I did not come down." She drew a breath. "It is my left. I write with the other."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-33.md:145:Nobody answered him. Cael had heard those words given, on a frozen road, by a square woman with her sleeves pushed up: that a man who stood a wall on that leg inside the month would keep the stick for the rest of his days. It was the eleventh day of thirty.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-33.md:156:Iron-Wall-adjacent. Vastin. Partial. Iron family. Held. A plane, not a body: the ground told not to give. Distinct from the third — Iron-adjacent, the bed; this is not the bed hardened, this is a line drawn on it and kept. Engagement field: defensive; rooted. Tier equivalent unknown. Deployment: none. Eleventh.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-33.md:159:Eleven.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-33.md:285:*Two hundred and ninetieth day; Treswick; the loft; a hundred and thirty-four. The cut, at dusk: six, hooded, two from the yard and four from the lane, with staves, one bow and one dark lantern, and no Path opened by any of them. Nobody dead, none taken, no faces. Karis: the left palm, on a step's edge; seven stitches, Brom's; no healer, since a healer here wants a name. Brom: both shoulders. Lira: the right shoulder, on a wall, and the arm did not take it. V.: a wall, on the eleventh day of thirty; the knee has gone again, and he cannot hold a bowl.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-33.md:291:*Deployment since the Line: thirty-two.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-33.md:295:*Eleventh. Iron Wall, from Vastin, in an alley, while he held a line for us with nothing behind him but the decision to. It's not Brom's — Brom gets harder, this holds. Since my Kindling I've learned to give ground and disappear. Now I've got the opposite in me, from the man who spent forty years being the wall they put in front of people like me. He held it for us instead. I don't have a word for what that is. I wrote it down anyway.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-33.md:305:She had fourteen letters, and three days left of a week that a man below had called his own. There was a plank of black oak propped against a table in the dark, two hundred yards under her head, and a bundle on a shelf above it that nobody had untied.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-27.md:239:"The loft's paid to the two hundred and eighty-eighth. A week from today wants two marks more, and I've got them. It's seven days of the hill, both ways." He looked at a bound leg. "And of that stair."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-28.md:3:The second card took them through two gates, on the two hundred and eighty-fifth day, a good deal more easily than the first.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-28.md:29:"Three boxes, corded. One surveyor's case, tarred. One courier's flat. One hide, rolled. Brought down for study on the two hundred and eighty-fourth." He read it from his own line, with his finger under it. Then he looked up, at the small pale woman on the other side of his ledge; and it was the first thing that he had ever asked any of them. "The same?"
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-28.md:287:*Two hundred and eighty-fifth day. Treswick; the loft. A hundred and thirty-six. Deployment since the Line: thirty-two. Lamp, from about the third hour. He says left and I go left.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-29.md:3:The dray came into the yard behind them, on the two hundred and eighty-sixth day, by the carts' gate at the bottom.
