   195	## Changes made while drafting (written after the draft)
   196	
   197	- **Chapter 27 has six scenes.** The last was divided at the clerk's bell. Seln's report at the loft is of the low door in the yard (which is what he can see), not of the iron door.
   198	- **Chapter 28.** The clerk settles his own book: *the same*, the day, and *four*. He asks one thing ("The same?"). Seln's reason for not lying is given by Seln, in the loft, as his own rule of the 282nd applied to himself.
   199	- **Chapter 29.** Karis gives no count of the kinds on the 286th: she will not say how many bear until all fifty-two are laid. The board's other three rows are found on the Stair's ninth sheet, the Ring's sixth and the Stair's twenty-first. Vastin holds the dray's mule by the cheek-strap and gives no order; afterward he says that he has followed fifty-two orders down a stair and not known his own trade.
   200	- **Chapter 30 has six scenes.** The cushion appears on the second chair on the 287th (the fourth day), not the third. Seln's fourth thought on the roof (to leave the case on an unticketed shelf in the Deepstacks) is seen for filing and put by. Cleon gives his week before the close and puts two fingers on the bundle without taking it down.
   201	- **Chapter 31.** Karis's count is given on the 288th: seven kinds bear, twenty-three are carried, eleven are nothing. Letters: eight from the board (the 288th, forenoon), two more from the Ring and the Hall (ten, the 288th), three from the Stair and the Hall (thirteen, the 289th), one from the Hall (fourteen, the 290th). She covers a word that is not a number, does not ask for the bundle, and does not show the page. Seln's second sighting is a porter on the kerb opposite the cut's head with a horseman's boots. Vastin holds three tall books at Lira's word and qualifies it ("I cannot undertake to carry them").
   202	- **Chapter 32.** Order going up: Vastin, Cael, Lira, Karis, Brom (so that Lira must pass Karis on the wet tread to reach the landing). Karis's gloves were in her pocket. The hood on the landing lifts two fingers and the lantern is raised for the wall itself; the cord takes the arm before the shutter opens. Compression rises as the old man falls and is told no: the catch is made with arms, a box and Brom's bound arm.
   203	- **Chapter 33.** Seven stitches. Brom re-laths the knee with a slat from his own box lid. Cael's ruling goes no farther than that the stair is not climbed at dusk again; the next day's route is left to Movement 6.
   204	- **Fragments, as written:** Anchor silent on the inner stair (ch27). The read asked in the yard at the dray (told no; ch29). In the alley all ten rose and were told no; Compression rose again at the fall and was told no (ch32). Shadow lifted at dusk on the 285th, the 286th and the 290th (told no). The eleventh asked three times (the step; the loft; the dark) and was told no each time. Nothing was used outward. Deployment thirty-two.

