editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-07.md:13:"I filed one once. My fourth year in the office. The district station in Ostrand had a frame that took to reading every Stone who stood in it a rank higher than he was. Not by much. Enough. A month of Stones went out of that station with ranks on their papers they hadn't earned, and nobody noticed until a quarryman's boy came up this hill with a certificate that said Rank Four and couldn't lift what a Rank Two lifts." He turned his folded hands over. "I wrote it up under the integrity provisions, because that's what they're for. They took the frame off its floor and tested it for a fortnight, and found a seam in the casing that let the damp in, and mended it, and read every Stone of that month over again. Then the frame went back on its floor and read true." He looked down the table at Cael. "That's an integrity question, in that volume. A frame that has drifted. You take it off the floor and test it until it reads true."
