editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-33.md:285:*Two hundred and ninetieth day; Treswick; the loft; a hundred and thirty-four. The cut, at dusk: six, hooded, two from the yard and four from the lane, with staves, one bow and one dark lantern, and no Path opened by any of them. Nobody dead, none taken, no faces. Karis: the left palm, on a step's edge; seven stitches, Brom's; no healer, since a healer here wants a name. Brom: both shoulders. Lira: the right shoulder, on a wall, and the arm did not take it. V.: a wall, on the eleventh day of thirty; the knee has gone again, and he cannot hold a bowl.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-33.md:295:*Eleventh. Iron Wall, from Vastin, in an alley, while he held a line for us with nothing behind him but the decision to. It's not Brom's — Brom gets harder, this holds. Since my Kindling I've learned to give ground and disappear. Now I've got the opposite in me, from the man who spent forty years being the wall they put in front of people like me. He held it for us instead. I don't have a word for what that is. I wrote it down anyway.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-33.md:299:*Not told. I can't tell the taking without telling the rest, and the rest is six people's. He asked for the wall to be entered, and I said that it was.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-30.md:159:*Brom was offered the life. He picked up the box.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-30.md:161:*Seln looked at it. Decided nothing.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-28.md:287:*Two hundred and eighty-fifth day. Treswick; the loft. A hundred and thirty-six. Deployment since the Line: thirty-two. Lamp, from about the third hour. He says left and I go left.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-28.md:291:*Karis has been looking for this room her whole life. Cleon's been sitting in it for thirty years waiting for her. Vastin tried to open a door with his rank and nearly closed all of them — an Archmarshal's worth nothing here, which he's taking about as well as I took [SHATTERED]. Down here the stone's older than the Compact, so the Compact doesn't reach. First place inside walls I've ever stood where nobody can file me, and it's a hole under a city, and it's because everything down here is older than the machine that files. Karis says give her a week. I've got a box to carry and a promise to keep about a station upstairs. I can wait.*
