     5	## Standing facts carried in
     6	
     7	- Forenoon of the 284th, on the stair's head inside the iron door under the registry. Below: Cael, Brom, Lira, Vastin, Karis; three boxes, the tarred kit case, the flat, the hide; Cleon with one lamp. The clerk outside. Seln above ground, on no card. Oryn two gates north with the brown mule.
     8	- Ten fragments. Deployment since the Line thirty-two. Shadow twice and sealed; Anchor's counted uses two; Tide on Oryn twice, on himself five times, nobody else. The still place read round and not in; untouched.
     9	- Purse 136. Reserve sealed in the third box (Cael's). Sixty yards of four-strand owed to the Lowmarch ferryman, to be bought going out. The loft is paid for a week from the 282nd.
    10	- Vastin: right knee lath-bound; the 284th is day five of thirty; stick; no kneeling, no running, NO WALL (Oryn: stand a wall on it inside the month and keep the stick for life). No age. He does not know the mechanism, what Cael carries, or the sum. He declined the second reading for the Ostrand case (causal) and was privately relieved.
    11	- Brom: two right toes, five days left on the 284th (done on the 289th); right shoulder in the older healer's webbing ("if it tells you anything, put down whatever you're carrying"); the left is the good one. Lira: arm day nineteen out of the wool on the 284th (day twenty-five on the 290th); slow; not to be fallen on; registry paper unshown.
    12	- Cleon's terms: all sheets in their places; they come down; no names; nobody tells him what the sheets are or how old until he has looked; one CARRIED lamp, his, held where he says; no other carried light and no fire of anybody's. He has seen one sheet and knows: three places, fifty-two sheets, fused grey floors with no join, older than what the Compact found. He has taken no notice of Cael. Rune Path, Bronze, by Seln's report; not shown.
    13	- Cards are good only for the day written on them, are counted with a pen at both upper gates and torn. The way: the load lane under the third wall (four alleys opening on the square) and the cut of twenty-two steps in five flights (from the top 5, 4, 4, 4, 5), a stride and a half wide, walled three men high, no door or window. On the fourth flight from the top (the second from the yard) one tread is worn to a dish and is wet.
    14	- The promise: not the steps, not the square. Cael has not looked at the crown. Lira keeps it unasked.
