59:"I told you to mind him on them; they are older than he is." He made his stroke. "Go on. I shall not write the lateness against the card, this once, since I should not care to explain that card to anybody."
61:---
73:"After the fourth bell there's the side door," said Lira. "With a card. It said so."
75:"*As the house's means allow.* A card is a figure, and a figure is seen when those with names have been seen. She would sit on that bench until the morning; and in the morning they would still ask her what she was."
81:"I have three days, and I have fourteen letters. If a paper is served on me tomorrow, at a registry's own yard door, then four people have carried fifty-two sheets up that hill for a week to no purpose, and a man below will never be told why I did not come down." She drew a breath. "It is my left. I write with the other."
127:---
145:Nobody answered him. Cael had heard those words given, on a frozen road, by a square woman with her sleeves pushed up: that a man who stood a wall on that leg inside the month would keep the stick for the rest of his days. It was the eleventh day of thirty.
159:Eleven.
179:---
227:So it was a debt, and of a kind that he had not carried before. He had owed a healer a telling, and had paid it. He owed this one, and could not pay; and the man had thanked him.
245:---
285:*Two hundred and ninetieth day; Treswick; the loft; a hundred and thirty-four. The cut, at dusk: six, hooded, two from the yard and four from the lane, with staves, one bow and one dark lantern, and no Path opened by any of them. Nobody dead, none taken, no faces. Karis: the left palm, on a step's edge; seven stitches, Brom's; no healer, since a healer here wants a name. Brom: both shoulders. Lira: the right shoulder, on a wall, and the arm did not take it. V.: a wall, on the eleventh day of thirty; the knee has gone again, and he cannot hold a bowl.*
291:*Deployment since the Line: thirty-two.*
305:She had fourteen letters, and three days left of a week that a man below had called his own. There was a plank of black oak propped against a table in the dark, two hundred yards under her head, and a bundle on a shelf above it that nobody had untied.

