+# Verdict
+
+**RATIFY WITH LINE FIXES.** The movement's architecture, event order, calendar, entry mechanics, money, bodies, alley outcome, fragment count and deployment count can stand. Apply the nine exact fixes at the end: five replace required `[[TIER-B]]` markers; two restore Cleon as the source speaker of "Give me a week" and repair that join; two remove the paraphrase-frame from the eleventh notice and give the notice the edition's established heading. No scene needs re-staging.
+
+The principal protected-text error is bounded but mandatory: the source makes Cleon—not Karis—the speaker of both "Being believed ..." and "Give me a week" (`source chapter-10.md:45`), while the draft assigns the first to a marker staged as Karis and the second directly to Karis (`manuscript/chapter-27.md:221,235`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:49,65`). The fixes preserve Karis's preceding request for time (`chapter-27.md:229–233`), so the protected S10 log's summary that Karis asks for a week remains true (`chapter-28.md:291`; `BOOK_MAP.md:400`).
+
+## 1. Continuity with the closed text
+
+### Entry seam, people and access
+
+- **PASS.** Movement 4 closes with Karis, Brom, Lira, Vastin and Cael inside the iron door, Cleon at its stair, and the clerk outside (`chapter-26.md:249–273`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:391–405`). Movement 5 begins on that same stair with Cleon, the five, the one carried lamp and the same loads (`chapter-27.md:3–19`). Seln remains above ground; he is neither on the card nor one of the four hands (`chapter-26.md:183–217`; `chapter-28.md:67–73,93–109`).
+- **PASS.** Karis is the unnamed bearer; Cael, Brom, Lira and Vastin are the four hands. Thus five people go below each day, not six. Seln is the sixth member of the party but stays above. The day card is renewed, Cleon writes the next one, and the clerk carries forward *the same* and *four* (`chapter-27.md:193–195`; `chapter-28.md:3–31,83–89`; `chapter-32.md:19`). This agrees with the closed count (`chapter-26.md:183–217`) and the one-day-card ruling (`STATE_LEDGER.md:392`).
+- **PASS.** Vastin speaks his old name, rank and office at the yard hatch, but the clerk lifts the pen away and writes only *The same* and *four* (`chapter-28.md:63–89`). Nothing says one of the four restricted names is written. Vastin is not one of those four in any event; the trigger remains unspent (`STATE_LEDGER.md:392`; `chapter-28.md:93–99`).
+- **PASS.** Seln's answer is truthful. After Fix 4 it says that Vastin is on the count, that the four hands are the same as the prior day, that Karis entered and answered for them, and that the form asks what a hand is for—not what he was (`source chapter-10.md:83`; marker at `chapter-28.md:73`). The prose expressly tests the statement and finds every word true; the cost is that the clerk now knows Seln's face and voice (`chapter-28.md:93–99`). Being off the 284th count did not require him to be absent from the yard on the 285th (`STATE_LEDGER.md:391–392`).
+
+### Loads, terms, objects and knowledge
+
+- **PASS.** The three boxes, tarred kit case, courier's flat and hide pass intact from the closed seam into the chamber (`chapter-26.md:183–217,255–269`; `chapter-27.md:17–19,113–121`). The first copies are laid 11/29/12 and remain on Cleon's three tables; the boxes travel up and down daily (`chapter-27.md:159–195`; `chapter-33.md:305`).
+- **PASS.** Cleon's terms hold. He receives all sheets in order, is told no theory before he looks, controls one carried lamp, and gets no second carried light or fire below (`chapter-26.md:255–269`; `chapter-27.md:3–17,159–195`; `chapter-29.md:193–215`). The flame Karis lights on the 288th is in the inn kitchen, not below (`chapter-31.md:3–17`). Brom does say Karis's name in Cleon's hearing, and Cleon objects; this is a consequence on the page, not a concealed breach (`chapter-29.md:221–233`).
+- **PASS.** Cael and Vastin retain exactly their closed mutual knowledge: Vastin knows the two failed readings and their stated limit, while Cael knows the Ostrand reason and Vastin's private relief; neither is promoted to friendship or given the mechanism (`chapter-21.md:121–223`; `chapter-33.md:191–227`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:395`). Vastin still does not learn of the eleventh (`chapter-33.md:223–227,299`).
+- **PASS, with planning correction noted.** The manuscript's *shut* is right for Seln's case (`chapter-30.md:35,73–79`). The map/packet's *unopened* inheritance is stale: Karis worked with the case open before five people in Book 6 and Seln later unlocked it again (`book-06 chapter-39.md:5,15,217`). Preserve **shut** and “contents not named in this movement”; do not restore *unopened*. The current scene exposes no contents (`chapter-30.md:73–85`).
+
+### Bodies, money and counts
+
+- **PASS.** Vastin enters day 284 on day five of Oryn's thirty, with the right knee bound and no wall permitted (`chapter-26.md:201–207`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:395`). Day 290 is day eleven. He knowingly breaks the no-wall order, the knee goes again, a lath cracks, the joint doubles in size, and he cannot stand or hold a bowl (`chapter-32.md:89–103`; `chapter-33.md:129–145,191–205,285`). The injury is worse but the month does not reset: it remains day eleven of the original thirty, with the threatened lasting stick now a live consequence (`chapter-33.md:145`; `BOOK_MAP.md:220,229,249`).
+- **PASS.** Brom's two right toes finish on the 289th (`chapter-31.md:265–271`). His older right-shoulder knot remains bound; the 286th dray spends the good left shoulder, and the 290th slab worsens it. He then carries the box on the bound shoulder, which Cael enters as debt (`chapter-29.md:45–125`; `chapter-32.md:117–137`; `chapter-33.md:285`). This does not contradict the older healer's knot or Oryn's fork order (`STATE_LEDGER.md:395`).
+- **PASS.** Lira reaches day twenty-five out of wool on the 290th. The alley bruises her right shoulder against the wall; the recovering left arm takes no load and does not fail (`chapter-32.md:141–159`; `chapter-33.md:285`; `BOOK_MAP.md:249`). Karis's left palm—not right—is cut on a step edge and receives seven stitches from Brom because a local healer would require a name (`chapter-32.md:161–171`; `chapter-33.md:63–125,285`).
+- **PASS.** Purse 136 becomes 134 when Brom pays two marks for the loft's second week on the 289th (`chapter-31.md:265–267`). That is the missing bridge in the map's cash track and lets Movement 6's four-mark meal leave 130 (`BOOK_MAP.md:249`; `MOVEMENT-006.md:38`). Deployment remains thirty-two throughout (`chapter-28.md:287`; `chapter-29.md:311`; `chapter-33.md:291`).
+
+No surviving prose contradiction with the closed chapters remains after the protected-text fixes below.
+
+## 2. Movement plan and all owner flags
+
+### Beat and withholding audit
+
+- **PASS, in order.** Deepstacks entry and the 11/29/12 laying precede the yard-door crisis; the chamber's external Rune demonstration precedes the decipherment; Brom's offer and Seln's night walk precede Cleon's 287th close; the 288th–290th letter work precedes the alley and the eleventh (`chapter-27.md:3–245`; `chapter-28.md:3–291`; `chapter-29.md:3–311`; `chapter-30.md:3–319`; `chapter-31.md:3–339`; `chapter-32.md:3–257`; `chapter-33.md:3–305`; plan order at `MOVEMENT-005.md:48–61`).
+- **PASS.** Cleon's Path is shown only from outside: his board, reed and “bearer/carried/nothing” result. There is no inside lean and no acquisition from him (`chapter-29.md:193–215,263–289`; `MOVEMENT-005.md:69`). Cael wants the instrument used on himself, records the wish and never says it (`chapter-29.md:281–289`; `chapter-31.md:243–249`).
+- **PASS.** Karis deciphers numerals and then letters only. She reads no non-number word, does not untie the bundle, does not read a leaf and does not show Vastin's page to Cleon (`chapter-31.md:63–189,319–339`; `chapter-32.md:3–19`). Nothing pre-empts the leaf's one reading on the 293rd or the grade/three marks/ages on the 298th (`MOVEMENT-006.md:39,48–53`; `BOOK_MAP.md:473`).
+- **PASS.** The eleventh arrives only in the alley's quiet middle minute after Cael has witnessed Iron Wall at the earlier cut and throughout this second earnest use; it is neither deployed nor told to Vastin, and no twelfth appears (`chapter-32.md:237–257`; `chapter-33.md:149–175,223–227,291–299`; `MOVEMENT-005.md:69–70`). This satisfies the universe rule that Cael must witness an ability in use (`UNIVERSE_BIBLE.md:222`). The earlier brief exposure yielded nothing; the prose draws no causal threshold (`STATE_LEDGER.md:389`; `chapter-32.md:241–251`).
+- **PASS.** Alley locks hold: Vastin roots wall to wall and “there is no round”; nobody else declares; Brom uses a step-stone; Lira drops and puts the knife into the stave; Cael stays at the plane's foot for the minute and is the reason; Seln takes the signal arm from the roof. None is taken, no face is secured, and nobody dies (`chapter-32.md:75–257`; `chapter-33.md:3–61,247–289`; `MOVEMENT-005.md:60–61`). The faction observes an ordinary rock, knife, cord and still boy as well as the wall, but sees nothing of quiet ground or what Cael carries (`chapter-33.md:249–275,287`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:121`).
+
+### Owner flags 1–19
+
+1. **AMEND.** The protected notice wording is exact, but its frame says Cael puts the lines into his own plain words and its fenced block omits the established `FRAGMENT ACQUIRED` heading (`chapter-33.md:153–157`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:131`). The last three edition acquisitions all stand as unframed system text under that heading (`book-06 chapter-32.md:23–32`; `book-06 chapter-54.md:141–152`; `book-07 chapter-37.md:171–184`). Apply Fixes 8–9.
+2. **KEEP.** The eleventh is acquired during sustained, earnest, close-range witnessed use, after a prior shorter witness produced nothing; no threshold is asserted (`chapter-32.md:217–257`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:132`; `UNIVERSE_BIBLE.md:222`). *This far?* is a permissible newly minted fragment prompt.
+3. **KEEP.** In the source, the antecedent of “it” is “what you are, on the paper,” not Oryn's order (`source chapter-12.md:123`). The draft matches: Vastin separates the knee as his first head, then says he knows only the plate's word for Cael before the protected sentence (`chapter-33.md:191–205`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:133`).
+4. **KEEP manuscript; amend future planning language.** *Shut* is canon; *unopened* is not. The case was open before five in Book 6 (`book-06 chapter-39.md:5,15,217`), and the M5 prose names no contents (`chapter-30.md:35,73–79`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:134`).
+5. **KEEP.** Seln may be off the research card/count and still pose as a porter on the hatch bench. His intervention is truthful, and the clerk's knowledge of his face is the paid cost (`chapter-28.md:3–19,67–99`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:135`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:391–392`).
+6. **KEEP.** The clerk's form has no clean line for matter taken up and returned; he asks one question and is about to consult the under-registrar before Seln supplies the true form answer (`chapter-28.md:23–45,73–89`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:136`). This does not spend the later lock that three other questions remain unasked by the 291st (`BOOK_MAP.md:476`).
+7. **KEEP.** Cleon's own week starts on the 287th. Its seventh day is the 293rd, and after the 290th there are three days—291, 292 and 293—left (`chapter-30.md:253–261`; `chapter-33.md:277,305`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:137`; `MOVEMENT-006.md:39`). The 284th protected line is also Cleon's after Fix 2, while Karis's preceding request explains the S10 log.
+8. **KEEP.** The second loft week costs two marks on the 289th, moving 136 to 134; Movement 6's four-mark meal then lands on the planned 130 (`chapter-31.md:265–267`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:138`; `BOOK_MAP.md:249`; `MOVEMENT-006.md:38`).
+9. **KEEP.** Seven bearer kinds, twenty-three carried kinds, eleven ornaments, and fourteen letters by the 290th do not disclose a non-number word, the leaf, the un-bound, “Made,” “For a kind,” the grade, three marks or ages (`chapter-31.md:71–189,319–339`; `chapter-32.md:3–19`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:139`; `MOVEMENT-006.md:39,46–53`).
+10. **KEEP.** Seln's inference—that the faction wanted a visible declaration and a carried box and avoided opening Paths because it too could be entered—is presented as a finding, not omniscient fact (`chapter-33.md:247–275,287`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:140`). It supplies the packet-required limit without disclosing faction identity (`MOVEMENT-005.md:61,72`).
+11. **KEEP.** Iron Wall is opened inside the third wall but within the blind cut; only the attackers and crew witness it. The narration does not claim what the crown sensed (`chapter-32.md:75–103`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:141`).
+12. **KEEP.** The notice says `Tier equivalent unknown`; it does not give Vastin a tier or age (`chapter-33.md:155–169`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:142`; protected wording at `BOOK_MAP.md:360`).
+13. **KEEP.** The iron handrail at the cut's mouth is expressly licensed by the map's private staging note; its absence from Movement 4's earlier description is not a contradiction (`chapter-32.md:79–81`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:143`; `BOOK_MAP.md:321–327`).
+14. **KEEP.** The uphill order Vastin, Cael, Lira, Karis, Brom is private alley staging and preserves every fixed action (`chapter-32.md:43–73`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:144`; `BOOK_MAP.md:321–327`).
+15. **KEEP.** Lira's claim that she fed Cael is already anchored by an explicit earlier event—she held the spoon on two successive nights when he could not hold it (`book-02 chapter-55.md:29–45`; `book-02 chapter-56.md:29–35`). The M5 line can also refer to the later Stair bill, where Shadow left his hands dead to the elbows (`book-07 chapter-51.md:7,199`; `chapter-33.md:135`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:145`). Nothing contradicts either occurrence.
+16. **KEEP.** The under-registrar, local returns hatch, three-door registry pattern and no-questions courier rule contradict no bible, closed chapter or later packet (`chapter-28.md:23–45`; `chapter-30.md:89–103`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:146`). Treat them as now-minted Compact institutional canon.
+17. **KEEP.** Lira's direction is qualified before Vastin complies, so he walks the order back as required (`chapter-31.md:283–293`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:147`; sequence lock at `BOOK_MAP.md:467`).
+18. **KEEP.** Cael rules only that they will not use the cut at dusk; he leaves the next route open for Movement 6's daylight handcart (`chapter-33.md:277–281`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:148`; `MOVEMENT-006.md:28`).
+19. **KEEP.** The reported length is 36,066 (approximately 36,070), about 3% above the approximate 35,000 target (`AUTHOR-REPORT.md:7–22,149`). Karis's cutaway is about 3,000 against a 2,500 guide, and the probe's total 2%/14% with chapters 30 and 32 highest is editorial information, not a canon or plan failure (`AUTHOR-REPORT.md:22,28`; `MOVEMENT-005.md:7,64`).
+
+## 3. Calendar
+
+- **284th:** chapter 27 begins directly below the door opened on the 284th (`chapter-26.md:221–273`; `chapter-27.md:3–59`; `BOOK_MAP.md:225`).
+- **285th:** chapter 28 names the day and the second card; the protected log closes it (`chapter-28.md:3,287–291`; `BOOK_MAP.md:226`).
+- **286th:** Brom's dray/offer and Cleon's board occur on chamber day three; Seln's walk follows that night (`chapter-29.md:3–17,175–193`; `chapter-30.md:3–151`; `BOOK_MAP.md:227`).
+- **287th:** the morning log, Cleon's week and close, and Vastin's four lamp movements land together (`chapter-30.md:159–177,239–273,287–309`; `BOOK_MAP.md:227`).
+- **288th–289th:** Karis reaches ten then thirteen letters; the second loft week is paid and Brom's toes finish on the 289th (`chapter-31.md:3–189,265–271`; `BOOK_MAP.md:228`).
+- **290th:** the fourteenth letter, dusk alley, left-hand cut and eleventh occur in that order (`chapter-32.md:3–19,43–257`; `chapter-33.md:3–175,285–305`; `BOOK_MAP.md:229`).
+
+The injury arithmetic also reconciles: Vastin day 1 is the 280th, so the 284th is day 5 and the 290th day 11 (`BOOK_MAP.md:220,249`); Lira day 1 is the 266th, so the 290th is day 25 (`BOOK_MAP.md:214,249`); Karis's cut on the 290th will be eight days old on the 298th (`BOOK_MAP.md:249`). No day-count contradiction found.
+
+## 4. Standing defaults and Reader Standard
+
+- **PASS.** No season name, month name, English weekday, metric unit, numbered span since the Kindling, or possessive construction such as “his Path” for Cael appears in chapters 27–33. Water-source uses of *spring* are not season names. The protected “I was fourteen. I'm nineteen.” gives ages, not a Kindling-year count (`chapter-30.md:305–309`; defaults at `OWNER-DECISIONS.md:24–25,148–149,157,178–180`).
+- **PASS.** Cael is nineteen (`chapter-30.md:309`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:105`). Vastin has no stated age; “forty years” is service rounding (`chapter-33.md:203`; `MOVEMENT-005.md:74`).
+- **PASS.** Cael never enters the square or station steps and never looks at the crown. Seln may look at the station light because the promise is Cael's; Cael remains in the lane/cut route (`chapter-28.md:3–19`; `chapter-30.md:89–109`; sequence lock at `BOOK_MAP.md:471`).
+- **PASS.** The violence remains legible to a thirteen-year-old without gore: impacts, a cut palm and stitching are concrete but restrained (`chapter-32.md:113–179`; `chapter-33.md:87–123`). The prose gates reported zero Reader Standard violations (`AUTHOR-REPORT.md:24–29`).
+
+## 5. Protected text
+
+### Required restorations
