+## 6. New canon minted
+
+The rulings below cover every item in `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:75–97`.
+
+1. **Deepstacks ground and galleries — KEEP.** The twenty-seven-step inner stair, three galleries, cross-way, shelving, old sorting tables, desk, shelf and local contents are author-owned geography (`chapter-27.md:5–121`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:75`; `MOVEMENT-005.md:76–78`). They do not alter the already-closed twenty-two-step exterior cut.
+2. **Clerk's bell — KEEP.** It is local procedure and contradicts no lock (`chapter-27.md:263–271`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:76`).
+3. **Daily loads/cards — KEEP.** Cleon's table rule, nightly box return and next-day card support the one-day-card ruling (`chapter-27.md:193–195`; `chapter-28.md:3–19`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:77`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:392`).
+4. **Karis's stone conclusion — KEEP.** “Cut first; dark lining second; town work third” advances the permitted physical observation without dating it (`chapter-27.md:39–43`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:78`).
+5. **Clerk's voice, form problem and under-registrar — KEEP.** Local institutional detail; no contradiction (`chapter-28.md:23–45,83–89`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:79`).
+6. **Seln's paid truth and roof watch — KEEP.** His face is the cost and the parapet watch follows from it (`chapter-28.md:93–99,251–279`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:80`).
+7. **Lamp practice — KEEP.** It remains Cleon's single carried lamp and gives Cael a labour role without acquiring Rune (`chapter-28.md:111–175`; `chapter-29.md:175–215`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:81`).
+8. **Chairs — KEEP.** Local furniture, no plot lock spent (`chapter-27.md:125–157`; `chapter-30.md:253–279`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:82`).
+9. **Cleon's habits, reed, counters, bridge looks and heard name — KEEP.** All are external observation of Rune; none reveals the lean (`chapter-27.md:125–199`; `chapter-29.md:193–289`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:83`).
+10. **Board — KEEP.** Its material, four rows, shelf history and row correspondences are compatible with the later Rune/leaf sequence (`chapter-29.md:175–193,263–277`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:84`; `UNIVERSE_BIBLE.md:244–245`).
+11. **Seven/twenty-three/eleven — KEEP.** The categories and totals neither decode a forbidden word nor anticipate the grade (`chapter-31.md:117–189`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:85`).
+12. **Cleon's week — KEEP.** Arithmetic verified in §3 (`chapter-30.md:253–261`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:86`).
+13. **Bundle — KEEP.** Tied, on Cleon's shelf, untouched and unread (`chapter-30.md:263–273`; `chapter-33.md:305`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:87`).
+14. **Decipherment method and figures — KEEP.** Numerals first, then fourteen letters, number words only; no later reveal is spent (`chapter-31.md:63–189,319–339`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:88`).
+15. **Brom's yard and broker's offer — KEEP.** The no-Path lift, four-marks-and-found offer, bound-shoulder box and stair exchange satisfy the packet without contradicting the family or healer history (`chapter-29.md:3–147`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:89`).
