   147	## 8. Next-movement inheritance not already carried by Packet 006
   148	
   149	Packet 006 carries the 291st, borrowed handcart, Karis's bound left hand, eleven fragments, and the fact that three clerk questions remain unasked (`MOVEMENT-006.md:26–28`). Its author must additionally inherit the following surviving particulars:
   150	
   151	- **Deepstacks geography and custody.** Inside the iron door: black sliding bar; twenty-seven dark-stone steps in three flights; a short cross-way; three side-by-side galleries. Middle gallery: roughly 110 strides, shelving to the roof, old sorting tables from ninety strides, Cleon's sloped desk and fixed lamp at the end, with cup/jar/brown-taped bundle/board shelf above. Eastern gallery: tall old-town ledgers and ladders. Western gallery: quarry material, where the board was found. Fifty-two first copies remain on three tables; the board is against the third and the bundle remains tied on the shelf (`chapter-27.md:5–121`; `chapter-30.md:263–273`; `chapter-33.md:305`).
   152	- **What has been deciphered and by whom.** Karis alone has fourteen of twenty-three letters; she can read figures and number-words only. She knows seven kinds bear, twenty-three are carried and eleven are ornament/nothing, that a bearer heads a run, and that board and floors repeat the same rows. She has covered one tempting six-sign group and has not guessed it. Vastin's copied page remains in her coat, unshown to Cleon (`chapter-31.md:63–189,319–339`; `chapter-32.md:3–19`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:111`).
   153	- **Cleon's knowledge and statements.** Cleon knows Karis's name and has used it once; he knows the hand, has externally demonstrated bearer/carried/ornament and “orders,” has stated both limits, has matched the same make, and has delivered the documentation/built-twice close. His week runs from the 287th through the 293rd. He has not noticed Cael, learned of the alley, shown the inside/lean, or acquired knowledge of the mechanism (`chapter-27.md:187–199`; `chapter-29.md:193–289`; `chapter-30.md:253–279`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:117`).
   154	- **The eleventh and its entry.** Iron-Wall-adjacent, from Vastin, partial/held/defensive/rooted, tier equivalent unknown, deployment none. Cael has read it, refused its *This far?* three times, deployed nothing, and told only the log; Lira has therefore read it. Vastin has not been told. Cael recorded both Vastin's requested wall entry and more than Vastin knows (`chapter-32.md:237–257`; `chapter-33.md:149–175,205–227,291–299`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:105,125`).
   155	- **Vastin.** Right knee, original day eleven of thirty: gone sideways again, re-lathed with one slat from Brom's box, twice its former size; on the night of the 290th he cannot stand or hold a bowl. He knowingly heard and broke Oryn's no-wall order and asks that she be told he heard. He has no office on the page, no stated age, and still knows nothing of the mechanism or eleventh (`chapter-33.md:129–145,185–227,285`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:115`).
   156	- **Karis.** Left palm has a long shallow cut and seven stitches, bound in a strip of Brom's shirt; she writes right-handed. No healer inside the gate has seen her. She has three days left of Cleon's week (`chapter-33.md:63–125,277,305`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:111`).
   157	- **Brom.** Toes are done. The older right shoulder remains bound; the left/good shoulder was wrenched under the dray and worsened by the alley slab, leaving neither arm raisable above the elbow. He carries his box on the bound right shoulder. He has effectively rejected the broker's four-marks-and-found guard post, but the factor heard only `I'll think on it.` Cael has entered the shoulders as a debt for the mill's healers (`chapter-29.md:45–147`; `chapter-31.md:265–271`; `chapter-32.md:117–137`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:109`).
   158	- **What the faction knows.** It knows the loft and has deliberately shown that knowledge. It saw Vastin's uncovered face and Iron Wall, plus a rock/knife/still boy, but no Path from another crew member, no face of its own was secured, and it saw nothing of quiet ground or Cael's fragments. Seln's finding is that it wanted a visible declaration and a carried box and avoided being entered itself (`chapter-33.md:247–289`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:121`).
   159	- **Inn, purse, count and day.** Six are in the long loft over the stable; it is paid through the 295th, with pot at dusk and seven bowls. Purse 134, reserve sealed in the third box. The below-ground daily count remains Karis as bearer plus four hands; Seln is never one of them. Night of day 290 is complete; Movement 6 opens day 291. The cut will not be climbed at dusk again, but no further route ruling has been made (`chapter-31.md:265–267`; `chapter-33.md:277–305`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:101–103,123`).
   160	- **Lira and remaining objects.** Lira is day twenty-five out of wool, has a bruised right shoulder, and the left arm took nothing. Three boxes, kit case, flat and hide are in the loft; the 291st card is there; the shortened watchman's stave is with Seln; two plain bolts remain in the cut; sixty yards of four-strand are still owed and Brom means to buy them going out (`chapter-33.md:285–307`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:107,123`).
   161	- **Seln and the case.** Seln is at the ladder head/roof watch, knows the same altered boots through three sightings, and has the better half of his cord and the stave. A Treswick clerk knows his face and voice. His case is on him and **shut**; five people know its contents from Book 6, but this movement names none. He looked at the registry/front-yard-returns-door choice and decided nothing (`chapter-30.md:3–151`; `chapter-33.md:183,247–275`; `book-06 chapter-39.md:5,15,217`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:113`).
