+# Verdict
+
+**RATIFY WITH LINE FIXES.** The movement's architecture, event order, calendar, entry mechanics, money, bodies, alley outcome, fragment count and deployment count can stand. Apply the ten exact fixes at the end: five replace required `[[TIER-B]]` markers; three repair pronoun/speaker joins around Cleon's restored lines; two remove the paraphrase-frame from the eleventh notice and give the notice the edition's established heading. No scene needs re-staging.
+
+The principal protected-text error is bounded but mandatory: the source makes Cleon—not Karis—the speaker of both "Being believed ..." and "Give me a week" (`source chapter-10.md:45`), while the draft assigns the first to a marker staged as Karis and the second directly to Karis (`manuscript/chapter-27.md:221,235`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:49,65`). The fixes preserve Karis's preceding request for time (`chapter-27.md:229–233`), so the protected S10 log's summary that Karis asks for a week remains true (`chapter-28.md:291`; `BOOK_MAP.md:400`).
+
+## 1. Continuity with the closed text
+
+### Entry seam, people and access
+
+- **PASS.** Movement 4 closes with Karis, Brom, Lira, Vastin and Cael inside the iron door, Cleon at its stair, and the clerk outside (`chapter-26.md:249–273`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:391–405`). Movement 5 begins on that same stair with Cleon, the five, the one carried lamp and the same loads (`chapter-27.md:3–19`). Seln remains above ground; he is neither on the card nor one of the four hands (`chapter-26.md:183–217`; `chapter-28.md:67–73,93–109`).
+- **PASS.** Karis is the unnamed bearer; Cael, Brom, Lira and Vastin are the four hands. Thus five people go below each day, not six. Seln is the sixth member of the party but stays above. The day card is renewed, Cleon writes the next one, and the clerk carries forward *the same* and *four* (`chapter-27.md:193–195`; `chapter-28.md:3–31,83–89`; `chapter-32.md:19`). This agrees with the closed count (`chapter-26.md:183–217`) and the one-day-card ruling (`STATE_LEDGER.md:392`).
+- **PASS.** Vastin speaks his old name, rank and office at the yard hatch, but the clerk lifts the pen away and writes only *The same* and *four* (`chapter-28.md:63–89`). Nothing says one of the four restricted names is written. Vastin is not one of those four in any event; the trigger remains unspent (`STATE_LEDGER.md:392`; `chapter-28.md:93–99`).
+- **PASS.** Seln's answer is truthful. After Fix 4 it says that Vastin is on the count, that the four hands are the same as the prior day, that Karis entered and answered for them, and that the form asks what a hand is for—not what he was (`source chapter-10.md:83`; marker at `chapter-28.md:73`). The prose expressly tests the statement and finds every word true; the cost is that the clerk now knows Seln's face and voice (`chapter-28.md:93–99`). Being off the 284th count did not require him to be absent from the yard on the 285th (`STATE_LEDGER.md:391–392`).
