+
+2. `manuscript/chapter-27.md`
+   old: `He had no answer for her. He had lain awake over this day, as she had, and he had been afraid on her account of one thing only: that a man would look at three floors and shake his head. It had not come into his mind to be afraid of the other.`
+   new: `Cael had no answer for her. He had lain awake over this day, as she had, and he had been afraid on her account of one thing only: that a man would look at three floors and shake his head. It had not come into his mind to be afraid of the other.`
+
+3. `manuscript/chapter-27.md`
+   old: `"Give me a week."`
+   new: `Cleon opened his eyes. "Give me a week."`
+
+4. `manuscript/chapter-27.md`
+   old: `Brom had the figures before she had shut her mouth.`
+   new: `Brom had the figures before the words had settled.`
+
+5. `manuscript/chapter-28.md`
+   old: `[[TIER-B: Seln: "He's on the count … the form asks what a hand's for, not what he was." — the plan quotes this unit with an elision; staged as Seln's answer to the clerk at the hatch, cutting across Vastin's unfinished sentence; coordinator to supply protected text]]`
+   new: `"He's on the count. Four hands, same as yesterday, entered by the practitioner and answered for by her, and the form asks what a hand's for, not what he was. The researcher's at your counter and she'll want to be told we're through," Seln said.`
+
+6. `manuscript/chapter-29.md`
+   old: `[[TIER-B: "They're orders." — the plan quotes this line whole but does not pin its speaker; staged here as Cleon's, said over the board and the Hall's fourth sheet; coordinator to supply protected text]]`
+   new: `Cleon said, "They're orders."`
+
+7. `manuscript/chapter-29.md`
+   old: `[[TIER-B: "Same make." — the plan quotes this line whole but does not pin its speaker; staged here as Cleon's, of the board and the three floors, after its fourth row is found; coordinator to supply protected text]]`
+   new: `Cleon said, "Same make."`
+
+8. `manuscript/chapter-30.md`
+   old: `[[TIER-B: Cleon's close (S11): "You've been reading the strata. Old, older, oldest — I know, I read your face, you've dated these past anything the Compact admits." … "Here's what the strata can't tell you. These aren't the ruins of something. This is the *documentation* of something. Somebody wrote these down so the thing could be *built the same way twice*." … "In thirty years I never had the stone to match the text. You walked in with three floors." … "I don't think you're going to like what you've found, Karis. I've had a piece of it for a decade and I've never once slept well since." — the plan quotes this speech in four pieces with elisions; staged as Cleon's, to Karis, at his desk at the end of the 287th, with the bundle untouched on its shelf; coordinator to supply protected text]]`
+   new: `"You've been reading the strata. Old, older, oldest — I know, I read your face, you've dated these past anything the Compact admits." He tapped the board. "Here's what the strata can't tell you. These aren't the ruins of something. This is the *documentation* of something. Somebody wrote these down so the thing could be *built the same way twice*." He sat back. "In thirty years I never had the stone to match the text. You walked in with three floors." A beat. "I don't think you're going to like what you've found, Karis. I've had a piece of it for a decade and I've never once slept well since."`
+
+9. `manuscript/chapter-33.md`
+   old: `The lines were where they had always been, and nobody under those slates could see them but himself. He took them as he had taken the last, on a healer's plank: slowly, from the top, putting each into the plain words in which he would have to write it.`
+   new: `The lines were where they had always been, and nobody under those slates could see them but himself. He read them as they came.`
+
+10. `manuscript/chapter-33.md`
+   old: `Iron-Wall-adjacent. Vastin. Partial. Iron family. Held. A plane, not a body: the ground told not to give. Distinct from the third — Iron-adjacent, the bed; this is not the bed hardened, this is a line drawn on it and kept. Engagement field: defensive; rooted. Tier equivalent unknown. Deployment: none. Eleventh.`
+   new: `FRAGMENT ACQUIRED\nIron-Wall-adjacent. Vastin. Partial. Iron family. Held. A plane, not a body: the ground told not to give. Distinct from the third — Iron-adjacent, the bed; this is not the bed hardened, this is a line drawn on it and kept. Engagement field: defensive; rooted. Tier equivalent unknown. Deployment: none. Eleventh.`

