11:- **PASS.** Movement 4 closes with Karis, Brom, Lira, Vastin and Cael inside the iron door, Cleon at its stair, and the clerk outside (`chapter-26.md:249–273`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:391–405`). Movement 5 begins on that same stair with Cleon, the five, the one carried lamp and the same loads (`chapter-27.md:3–19`). Seln remains above ground; he is neither on the card nor one of the four hands (`chapter-26.md:183–217`; `chapter-28.md:67–73,93–109`).
12:- **PASS.** Karis is the unnamed bearer; Cael, Brom, Lira and Vastin are the four hands. Thus five people go below each day, not six. Seln is the sixth member of the party but stays above. The day card is renewed, Cleon writes the next one, and the clerk carries forward *the same* and *four* (`chapter-27.md:193–195`; `chapter-28.md:3–31,83–89`; `chapter-32.md:19`). This agrees with the closed count (`chapter-26.md:183–217`) and the one-day-card ruling (`STATE_LEDGER.md:392`).
13:- **PASS.** Vastin speaks his old name, rank and office at the yard hatch, but the clerk lifts the pen away and writes only *The same* and *four* (`chapter-28.md:63–89`). Nothing says one of the four restricted names is written. Vastin is not one of those four in any event; the trigger remains unspent (`STATE_LEDGER.md:392`; `chapter-28.md:93–99`).
14:- **PASS.** Seln's answer is truthful. After Fix 5 it says that Vastin is on the count, that the four hands are the same as the prior day, that Karis entered and answered for them, and that the form asks what a hand is for—not what he was (`source chapter-10.md:83`; marker at `chapter-28.md:73`). The prose expressly tests the statement and finds every word true; the cost is that the clerk now knows Seln's face and voice (`chapter-28.md:93–99`). Being off the 284th count did not require him to be absent from the yard on the 285th (`STATE_LEDGER.md:391–392`).
20:- **PASS.** Cael and Vastin retain exactly their closed mutual knowledge: Vastin knows the two failed readings and their stated limit, while Cael knows the Ostrand reason and Vastin's private relief; neither is promoted to friendship or given the mechanism (`chapter-21.md:121–223`; `chapter-33.md:191–227`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:395`). Vastin still does not learn of the eleventh (`chapter-33.md:223–227,299`).
25:- **PASS.** Vastin enters day 284 on day five of Oryn's thirty, with the right knee bound and no wall permitted (`chapter-26.md:201–207`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:395`). Day 290 is day eleven. He knowingly breaks the no-wall order, the knee goes again, a lath cracks, the joint doubles in size, and he cannot stand or hold a bowl (`chapter-32.md:89–103`; `chapter-33.md:129–145,191–205,285`). The injury is worse but the month does not reset: it remains day eleven of the original thirty, with the threatened lasting stick now a live consequence (`chapter-33.md:145`; `BOOK_MAP.md:220,229,249`).
26:- **PASS.** Brom's two right toes finish on the 289th (`chapter-31.md:265–271`). His older right-shoulder knot remains bound; the 286th dray spends the good left shoulder, and the 290th slab worsens it. He then carries the box on the bound shoulder, which Cael enters as debt (`chapter-29.md:45–125`; `chapter-32.md:117–137`; `chapter-33.md:285`). This does not contradict the older healer's knot or Oryn's fork order (`STATE_LEDGER.md:395`).
39:- **PASS.** The eleventh arrives only in the alley's quiet middle minute after Cael has witnessed Iron Wall at the earlier cut and throughout this second earnest use; it is neither deployed nor told to Vastin, and no twelfth appears (`chapter-32.md:237–257`; `chapter-33.md:149–175,223–227,291–299`; `MOVEMENT-005.md:69–70`). This satisfies the universe rule that Cael must witness an ability in use (`UNIVERSE_BIBLE.md:222`). The earlier brief exposure yielded nothing; the prose draws no causal threshold (`STATE_LEDGER.md:389`; `chapter-32.md:241–251`).
40:- **PASS.** No healer works inside the gate; Brom supplies the hand care because the local house would write a name, while Oryn remains north and off-page (`chapter-33.md:63–125`; `MOVEMENT-005.md:73`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:404`). Vastin learns neither the integration mechanism nor his age on the page (`chapter-33.md:191–227`; `MOVEMENT-005.md:74`).
49:5. **KEEP.** Seln may be off the research card/count and still pose as a porter on the hatch bench. His intervention is truthful, and the clerk's knowledge of his face is the paid cost (`chapter-28.md:3–19,67–99`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:135`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:391–392`).
120:3. **Daily loads/cards — KEEP.** Cleon's table rule, nightly box return and next-day card support the one-day-card ruling (`chapter-27.md:193–195`; `chapter-28.md:3–19`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:77`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:392`).

