26:**Cael knows:** ten fragments with current costs/deployment notes; deployment since the Line is 27. The still place is a location under the breastbone, read three times, with all ten going round it and none through; `Not the Quiet. Not a fragment.` He has obeyed the no-touch order. Four sites lie on one map edge: Ring, Stair and Hall entered; fourth unentered, unnamed, undated and untested at 440 yards and two strides radius behind stake 34 repeated one per pace. The three entered sites stop live Arbiters while his already-dark Arbiter remains dark and his fragments answer. He has no Path; nobody knows why. He knows the kit's radius line, 41-kind index, stroke/bar and `third site confirmed on bearing`; Karis's `Someone made this pattern.` remains unanswered.
121:- **Seam with the locked Book 7 ratified** (Sol plan audit): day 131 at Lowmarch; the five; ten fragments; the debt to Oryn paid, not forgiven; the still place told and here neither read nor touched; the fourth site unentered and untested; the kit, the dead man's ledger and fifty-two sheets; the brown mule with the five.
290:- **Ledger state.** It is the night before day 278; crew purse 118 marks; deployment thirty; ten fragments; Shadow still sealed after two prior uses; Anchor still two counted uses; Tide unused here; still place untouched (`manuscript/chapter-08.md:151–153`; `manuscript/chapter-09.md:263–265`; `manuscript/chapter-12.md:291–295`). Cael has not touched the page and has promised a daylight ruling at the plank with hands (`manuscript/chapter-12.md:223–241,267–299`).
300:- **Deployment since the Line: THIRTY-TWO**, both on the 279th at the cut: one grain of Ember at the mark (thirty-one; the heat came home along the left arm) and one Wind burst **away**, ten strides, to the north bank inside the wall (thirty-two). Pressure, Anchor, Edge, Storm and the read refused there. Shadow held, twice and sealed; Tide unused; no self-reading; Oryn has not read Cael. **Ten fragments: nothing came of standing two feet from the wall; the eleventh has not come.**
385:- **Progression:** ten fragments, deployment THIRTY-TWO (coordinator ruling: one Ember grain at the mark and one Wind burst away, both at the cut); Shadow sealed, Anchor still two, Tide unused, no self-read, no eleventh (`manuscript/chapter-15.md:133–163,223–227`; `manuscript/chapter-16.md:205–211`). Vastin has shown Iron Wall once; Cael witnessed it but did not acquire it (`packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:55`; `packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:52`).
394:- **Entry seam with Movement 3 ratified** (Sol plan audit): day 281 going down off the rise; six and no mule; the loads; deployment thirty-two; ten fragments; purse 138; bodies; the papers with Karis (the flat, the hide, the copied page in oilcloth, the dead surveyor's ledger, her notebook).
396:- **The reading inward (the 281st): the fourth and fifth self-readings**, with Tide, ROUND the still place and never in; **not counted** ("Myself, twice: not counted, as before"); a palm on a gatepost while it was open is a trial. Finding (protected): "He had been putting a cord on a stone and writing down *no length*." — the tenth feels only what flows; where nothing flows it returns nothing, and that nothing is the instrument's limit, not a finding about the place (a gatepost and the middle of himself come back alike). **He needs an instrument for what does not move.** He read Oryn's order for the leave he wanted, has logged that, and **owes her the telling at the mill before anything else is said**. Lira asked and is entered as having asked. **Deployment since the Line: thirty-two; ten fragments; none acquired.**
397:- **Vastin and Cael at the three-mile post.** Vastin SAT for the first time since the cut, of his own choosing, where he could not rise without Cael's arm. "I read your file" (no span of years). Cael: "You were the instrument," … "I was the error." (protected, Cael's). **Why he declined** (the author's, amended to locked Book 6): the case shown him at Ostrand is the true and causal reason — the office had shown him what it did with honest readings; and privately part of him was relieved never to learn what a plate would say (a second silence would have been turned on Cael; a plate that lit would have been turned on nine thousand of his own readings). A sound act, and glad of it for a bad reason. **What Cael gave him:** that the place has been read twice that day with "the one thing I've got that reads", and nothing came back because that thing only feels what moves. NOT what reads, nor fragments, the mechanism, the date. Vastin did not ask. "It is a place where two people can stand": ground, not friendship. The S7 log verbatim ("color" stands).
398:- **Treswick (the 282nd).** The grey bridge on five piers is of dark, dry-laid stone with no mortar and is OLDER than the walls (Karis, from the masons' fitting of the pale stone to it); the same dark stone is the registry's three lowest courses, the undercroft's end and the frame of the iron door. The outer gate: one keeper counts feet on a bead-frame ("Six"); another writes only loads that come on wheels to be sold. **No name of the six was written.** The outer district works by brokers' slate boards and counted labour: cards with a coloured edge (blue to the second wall, buff to the third) carry a figure, are counted in with a pen and torn at each gate, and are good for the day named. **Iron passes the second wall by right, Bronze the third** — on a certificate that is read out and WRITTEN. The smith's two forges (charcoal; an Ember's held bed for a horse with a blue band): Brom, "They shoe by the tier." (protected). The rope-walk: sixty yards of four-strand priced (no figure printed) and to be bought going out; the Lowmarch debt stands. **The inn with two doors** (the painted door has a book; the yard half-door takes money): the long loft over the stable for a week from the 282nd, the pot at dusk, seven bowls; two marks paid; **purse 136**. Lira hung a blanket over the loft's uphill window.
399:- **Vastin:** "I have papers I will not show. I want that said once, so that nobody asks twice." (three sheets under one seal, in oilskin, beside Karis's receipt). He has certified Treswick on four occasions. His cutaway: "the first honest district". He has sat three times; no age; no wall; **the right knee is day five of thirty on the 284th**; he came down twenty-two steps and caught one slip with his left hand.
445:**Brom.** Iron Skin; Copper. No grey. Right shoulder in the older healer's knot (it has not spoken). Right foot: five days left on the 284th; he favours it on hills. One box, with Oryn's bowl under its lashing. **The purse: a hundred and thirty-six.** Pike's thumbed slip in his shirt. He has looked at four-strand and will take it "going out". He lays seven bowls.
473:- **Day and bodies.** It is the forenoon of the 284th. Vastin's right knee is day five of thirty, still stiff, with stick/no kneeling/no running/no wall; he has now sat three times and descended twenty-two steps, catching one slip with his left hand. Brom has five days left on the two right toes and the older shoulder knot; Lira's arm is day nineteen out of wool and has carried the box with both arms. Cael is sound apart from the box strap (`ch25:87,197–205`; `ch26:47–127,153`; `AUTHOR-REPORT:103,105,107,113`).
475:- **Vastin and Cael.** Vastin has confessed both the sound institutional reason for refusing certification and his private relief at not learning what another plate would say. Cael has given him the fact of two self-readings and the instrument's limit, but not what reads, fragments, mechanism, date or arithmetic. Each holds one fact from the other; the relationship is explicitly ground, not friendship (`ch21:121–223` after fix 4).
478:**Movement 4 CLOSED (2026-10-11).** Same-author repair r1 (a bounded line repair; nothing re-staged): the nine coordinator-applied fixes kept and their joins smoothed (the boulder image made to agree with "*no length*"; Karis looks at three boxes and a case before "Four hands."; the cook-house questions after the restored exchange are of method only; "Four." given to Cael at the parapet); Vastin's refusal recomposed to locked Book 6 (the Ostrand case stated as the cause, twice, and not taken back; beside it "I had kept my hand off a door for a sound reason, and I was thankful of it for a poor one"; entered "on a form which has no line for why"); the two tracked passages in ch26 re-ordered (Lira prices the ladder aloud and shoulders the box before Cael understands; the clerk writes *four* and blots it before he looks at a face, then opens the door, looks at Vastin, opens his mouth and shuts it); Wind's ceiling removed; **Cleon's name comes to Cael at the cook-house counter and is then read on the card — nobody has said it aloud**; second tellings of the name-versus-count idea trimmed. Sol recheck: CLOSE WITH LINE FIXES; both tracked passages RESOLVED; every binding ruling borne out; the day arithmetic confirmed (161 days since the last self-reading; four days since the board; 282 days since the first sill; Oryn's gates). One punctuation fix applied by the coordinator (a broken dialogue join in ch21). The "New canon minted" and "State at movement end" sections above were refreshed from the post-repair author report. Final: 35,179 prose words; gates 0; overlap 0 unprotected (12 protected). Purse 136 marks; deployment thirty-two; ten fragments; the forenoon of day 284, inside the iron door under Treswick.

