+# Verdict
+
+**RATIFY WITH LINE FIXES.** The movement's architecture, event order, calendar, entry mechanics, money, bodies, alley outcome, fragment count and deployment count can stand. Apply the ten exact fixes at the end: five replace required `[[TIER-B]]` markers; three repair pronoun/speaker joins around Cleon's restored lines; two remove the paraphrase-frame from the eleventh notice and give the notice the edition's established heading. No scene needs re-staging.
+
+The principal protected-text error is bounded but mandatory: the source makes Cleon—not Karis—the speaker of both "Being believed ..." and "Give me a week" (`source chapter-10.md:45`), while the draft assigns the first to a marker staged as Karis and the second directly to Karis (`manuscript/chapter-27.md:221,235`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:49,65`). The fixes preserve Karis's preceding request for time (`chapter-27.md:229–233`), so the protected S10 log's summary that Karis asks for a week remains true (`chapter-28.md:291`; `BOOK_MAP.md:400`).
+
+## 1. Continuity with the closed text
+
+### Entry seam, people and access
+
+- **PASS.** Movement 4 closes with Karis, Brom, Lira, Vastin and Cael inside the iron door, Cleon at its stair, and the clerk outside (`chapter-26.md:249–273`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:391–405`). Movement 5 begins on that same stair with Cleon, the five, the one carried lamp and the same loads (`chapter-27.md:3–19`). Seln remains above ground; he is neither on the card nor one of the four hands (`chapter-26.md:183–217`; `chapter-28.md:67–73,93–109`).
+- **PASS.** Karis is the unnamed bearer; Cael, Brom, Lira and Vastin are the four hands. Thus five people go below each day, not six. Seln is the sixth member of the party but stays above. The day card is renewed, Cleon writes the next one, and the clerk carries forward *the same* and *four* (`chapter-27.md:193–195`; `chapter-28.md:3–31,83–89`; `chapter-32.md:19`). This agrees with the closed count and one-day-card ruling (`chapter-26.md:183–217`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:398,402`).
+- **PASS.** Vastin speaks his old name, rank and office at the yard hatch, but the clerk lifts the pen away and writes only *The same* and *four* (`chapter-28.md:63–89`). Nothing says one of the four restricted names is written. Vastin is not one of those four in any event; the trigger remains unspent (`STATE_LEDGER.md:402`; `chapter-28.md:93–99`).
+- **PASS.** Seln's answer is truthful. After Fix 5 it says that Vastin is on the count, that the four hands are the same as the prior day, that Karis entered and answered for them, and that the form asks what a hand is for—not what he was (`source chapter-10.md:83`; marker at `chapter-28.md:73`). The prose expressly tests the statement and finds every word true; the cost is that the clerk now knows Seln's face and voice (`chapter-28.md:93–99`). Being off the 284th count did not require him to be absent from the yard on the 285th (`STATE_LEDGER.md:402–403`).
+
+### Loads, terms, objects and knowledge
+
+- **PASS.** The three boxes, tarred kit case, courier's flat and hide pass intact from the closed seam into the chamber (`chapter-26.md:183–217,255–269`; `chapter-27.md:17–19,113–121`). The first copies are laid 11/29/12 and remain on Cleon's three tables; the boxes travel up and down daily (`chapter-27.md:159–195`; `chapter-33.md:305`).
+- **PASS.** Cleon's terms hold. He receives all sheets in order, is told no theory before he looks, controls one carried lamp, and gets no second carried light or fire below (`chapter-26.md:255–269`; `chapter-27.md:3–17,159–195`; `chapter-29.md:193–215`). The flame Karis lights on the 288th is in the inn kitchen, not below (`chapter-31.md:3–17`). Brom does say Karis's name in Cleon's hearing, and Cleon objects; this is a consequence on the page, not a concealed breach (`chapter-29.md:221–233`).
+- **PASS.** Cael and Vastin retain exactly their closed mutual knowledge: Vastin knows the two failed readings and their stated limit, while Cael knows the Ostrand reason and Vastin's private relief; neither is promoted to friendship or given the mechanism (`chapter-21.md:121–223`; `chapter-33.md:191–227`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:397,475`). Vastin still does not learn of the eleventh (`chapter-33.md:223–227,299`).
+- **PASS, with planning correction noted.** The manuscript's *shut* is right for Seln's case (`chapter-30.md:35,73–79`). The map/packet's *unopened* inheritance is stale: the five were present for the case material, Karis worked with the case open, and Seln later unlocked it again (`book-06 chapter-38.md:167`; `book-06 chapter-39.md:5,15,217`). Preserve **shut** and “contents not named in this movement”; do not restore *unopened*. The current scene exposes no contents (`chapter-30.md:73–85`).
+
+### Bodies, money and counts
+
+- **PASS.** Vastin enters day 284 on day five of Oryn's thirty, with the right knee bound and no wall permitted (`chapter-26.md:201–207`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:399,473`). Day 290 is day eleven. He knowingly breaks the no-wall order, the knee goes again, a lath cracks, the joint doubles in size, and he cannot stand or hold a bowl (`chapter-32.md:89–103`; `chapter-33.md:129–145,191–205,285`). The injury is worse but the month does not reset: it remains day eleven of the original thirty, with the threatened lasting stick now a live consequence (`chapter-33.md:145`; `BOOK_MAP.md:220,229,249`).
+- **PASS.** Brom's two right toes finish on the 289th (`chapter-31.md:265–271`). His older right-shoulder knot remains bound; the 286th dray spends the good left shoulder, and the 290th slab worsens it. He then carries the box on the bound shoulder, which Cael enters as debt (`chapter-29.md:45–125`; `chapter-32.md:117–137`; `chapter-33.md:285`). This does not contradict the older healer's knot or Oryn's fork order (`STATE_LEDGER.md:445,473`).
+- **PASS.** Lira reaches day twenty-five out of wool on the 290th. The alley bruises her right shoulder against the wall; the recovering left arm takes no load and does not fail (`chapter-32.md:141–159`; `chapter-33.md:285`; `BOOK_MAP.md:249`). Karis's left palm—not right—is cut on a step edge and receives seven stitches from Brom because a local healer would require a name (`chapter-32.md:161–171`; `chapter-33.md:63–125,285`).
+- **PASS.** Purse 136 becomes 134 when Brom pays two marks for the loft's second week on the 289th (`chapter-31.md:265–267`). That is the missing bridge in the map's cash track and lets Movement 6's four-mark meal leave 130 (`BOOK_MAP.md:249`; `MOVEMENT-006.md:38`). Deployment remains thirty-two throughout (`chapter-28.md:287`; `chapter-29.md:311`; `chapter-33.md:291`).
+
+No surviving prose contradiction with the closed chapters remains after the protected-text fixes below.
+
+## 2. Movement plan and all owner flags
+
+### Beat and withholding audit
+
+- **PASS, in order.** Deepstacks entry and the 11/29/12 laying precede the yard-door crisis; the chamber's external Rune demonstration precedes the decipherment; Brom's offer and Seln's night walk precede Cleon's 287th close; the 288th–290th letter work precedes the alley and the eleventh (`chapter-27.md:3–245`; `chapter-28.md:3–291`; `chapter-29.md:3–311`; `chapter-30.md:3–319`; `chapter-31.md:3–339`; `chapter-32.md:3–257`; `chapter-33.md:3–305`; plan order at `MOVEMENT-005.md:48–61`).
+- **PASS.** Cleon's Path is shown only from outside: his board, reed and “bearer/carried/nothing” result. There is no inside lean and no acquisition from him (`chapter-29.md:193–215,263–289`; `MOVEMENT-005.md:69`). Cael wants the instrument used on himself, records the wish and never says it (`chapter-29.md:281–289`; `chapter-31.md:243–249`).
+- **PASS.** Karis deciphers numerals and then letters only. She reads no non-number word, does not untie the bundle, does not read a leaf and does not show Vastin's page to Cleon (`chapter-31.md:63–189,319–339`; `chapter-32.md:3–19`). Nothing pre-empts the leaf's one reading on the 293rd or the grade/three marks/ages on the 298th (`MOVEMENT-006.md:39,48–53`; `BOOK_MAP.md:473`).
+- **PASS.** The eleventh arrives only in the alley's quiet middle minute after Cael has witnessed Iron Wall at the earlier cut and throughout this second earnest use; it is neither deployed nor told to Vastin, and no twelfth appears (`chapter-32.md:237–257`; `chapter-33.md:149–175,223–227,291–299`; `MOVEMENT-005.md:69–70`). This satisfies the universe rule that Cael must witness an ability in use (`UNIVERSE_BIBLE.md:222`). The earlier brief exposure yielded nothing; the prose draws no causal threshold (`STATE_LEDGER.md:300,385`; `chapter-32.md:241–251`).
+- **PASS.** No healer works inside the gate; Brom supplies the hand care because the local house would write a name, while Oryn remains north and off-page (`chapter-33.md:63–125`; `MOVEMENT-005.md:73`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:404`). Vastin learns neither the integration mechanism nor his age on the page (`chapter-33.md:191–227`; `MOVEMENT-005.md:74`).
+- **PASS.** Alley locks hold: Vastin roots wall to wall and “there is no round”; nobody else declares; Brom uses a step-stone; Lira drops and puts the knife into the stave; Cael stays at the plane's foot for the minute and is the reason; Seln takes the signal arm from the roof. None is taken, no face is secured, and nobody dies (`chapter-32.md:75–257`; `chapter-33.md:3–61,247–289`; `MOVEMENT-005.md:60–61`). The faction observes an ordinary rock, knife, cord and still boy as well as the wall, but sees nothing of quiet ground or what Cael carries (`chapter-33.md:249–275,287`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:121`).
+
+### Owner flags 1–19
+
+1. **AMEND.** The protected notice wording is exact, but its frame says Cael puts the lines into his own plain words and its fenced block omits the established `FRAGMENT ACQUIRED` heading (`chapter-33.md:153–157`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:131`). The last three edition acquisitions all stand as unframed system text under that heading (`book-06 chapter-32.md:23–32`; `book-06 chapter-54.md:141–152`; `book-07 chapter-37.md:171–184`). Apply Fixes 9–10.
